    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5555?c=usm": {
      "title": "Post Doctoral Research Associate",
      "description": "Post Doctoral Research Associate | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Post Doctoral Research Associate Gulfport, MS, United States | req5555 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/7/2026 Back to Search Post Doctoral Research Associate The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Post Doctoral Research Associate. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date November 30, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Post-Doctoral Research Associate conducts and\nleads research in ocean observing networks, uncrewed systems, and data science\nwithin the Roger F. Wicker Center for Ocean Enterprise. This position\nintegrates fundamental engineering principles and data science methods to\nsupport autonomous data collection, sensor algorithm development, marine\nenvironmental modeling, and research, development, testing, and evaluation\n(RDT&E) of uncrewed systems (UxS) and ocean observing technologies. The\nposition develops and implements statistical, mathematical, computer\nprogramming, operations research, and diagnostic methods and techniques to\ninterpret and analyze complex data. Exercising independent judgment under\nlimited supervision from a higher-level scientist or technical supervisor, the\nPost-Doctoral Research Associate supports research involving ocean sensing\nbuoys and uncrewed surface and subsurface marine vehicles, including platform\nsystems, payloads, command and control systems, power systems, and data\nintegration and analysis. This position is located at the Roger F. Wicker\nCenter for Ocean Enterprise in Gulfport, Mississippi, and collaborates with\nindustry, academic, state, and federal partners to advance ocean technology and\nresearch initiatives. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Conducts independent and collaborative research to advance hardware, software, and techniques and develops computational algorithms and statistical methods to identify patterns and relationships in large volumes of data. Prepares technical reports, peer-reviewed publications, and presentations to communicate research findings and innovation outcomes. Collaborates with academic and external partners to support research initiatives and expand project impact. Contributes to Ocean Enterprise goals by participating in the development of proposals, keeping appropriate Ocean Enterprise staff informed of activities, and providing status reports documenting project milestones. Participates in the testing and evaluation of uncrewed systems (UxS) and other autonomous or semi-autonomous vehicles or platforms and performs analysis of collected data. Provides programmatic and technical support to project directors or principal investigators and collaborates with Ocean Enterprise, The University of Southern Mississippi, and external researchers, as appropriate. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D.\nfrom an accredited college or university in Oceanography, Data Science, Ocean\nEngineering, Hydrography, Physical Science or a related field. Dissertation\nmust be defended and approved, and all degree requirements must be met prior to\nthe start of the position. Two (2) years of experience in data science\nresearch, applications, or a similar occupation. Related education and related\nexperience may be substituted on an equal basis. Must have a valid Driver’s\nLicense. Must be able to obtain Transportation Worker Identification Credential\n(TWIC). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to read, analyze, and interpret research periodicals, professional journals, and technical procedures associated with research activities. Strong written communication skills with the ability to prepare technical documentation, reports, research findings, and related materials. Ability to organize, document, and manage experimental data in accordance with research standards and established procedures. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from data science professionals, stakeholders, and the public. Ability to process, visualize, analyze, and interpret various geospatial datasets and perform fieldwork aboard small and large vessels, as required. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret research periodicals, professional journals, and technical procedures associated with research activities. Strong written communication skills with the ability to prepare technical documentation, reports, research findings, and related materials. Ability to organize, document, and manage experimental data in accordance with research standards and established procedures. Ability to effectively present information and respond to questions from data science professionals, stakeholders, and the public. Ability to process, visualize, analyze, and interpret various geospatial datasets and perform fieldwork aboard small and large vessels, as required. Knowledge of programming languages, platforms, software libraries, databases, cloud computing environments, and analytical tools used in data science and research, including Python, Java, Robot Operating System (ROS), R and RStudio, MATLAB, Amazon Web Services SageMaker, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, TensorFlow, Keras, Scikit-learn, Pandas, BASH, Apache, Parquet, Protocol Buffers, Nginx, NumPy, SQL, NoSQL databases including MongoDB, ArcPy, Tableau, Docker, and ArcGIS. Preferred Qualifications Two\n(2) years of experience in Uncrewed vehicles, Marine data science or related\nresearch. Two (2) years of experience preparing or contributing to\npeer-reviewed manuscripts, grant proposals, or conference presentations. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
