    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5605?c=usm": {
      "title": "Dean - College of Education and Human Sciences",
      "description": "Dean - College of Education and Human Sciences | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Dean - College of Education and Human Sciences Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5605 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/6/2026 Back to Search Dean - College of Education and Human Sciences The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Dean - College of Education and Human Sciences. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division College of Education and Human Sciences Position Type Administrative Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a\ncover letter addressing their qualifications and interest in the dean position,\na current curriculum vitae, a brief statement of leadership philosophy and\nexperience, and contact information for three professional references. For full\nconsideration, applications must be submitted by January 6, 2027. \nAdditional materials may be requested at a later date.  Questions may be\ndirected to the search committee chair, Dr. Chris Winstead (Chris.Winstead@usm.edu). Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Dean provides\nadministrative oversight and leadership for the college, serving as its chief\nexecutive and academic officer as it grows and evolves to meet the educational\nneeds of the University. As a collaborative leader, the Dean works alongside\nSchool Directors and faculty to champion student success and faculty\nachievement across teaching, research, creative activity, service, and economic\ndevelopment. The role offers the opportunity to shape the college's future\nwhile balancing strategic growth with responsible resource management. Offering a\nnumber of highly ranked and nationally accredited programs, the College of\nEducation and Human Sciences (CEHS) is home to six thriving schools, including\nthe schools of Education, Human Development and Family Science, Kinesiology and\nNutrition, Library and Information Science, Psychology, and Social Work.  CEHS\nprepares both traditional and non-traditional students with innovative\ncurricula and field experiences through our 12 undergraduate and 20 graduate\nprograms across Hattiesburg, Gulf Park (GP), and online campuses. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provides leadership for and\n     management of the college's day-to-day operations, including active\n     engagement in shared governance, oversight of faculty and staff\n     recruitment, strategic workload management, and the promotion of\n     organizational alignment and effectiveness across Schools and Colleges. Ensures adherence to institutional principles regarding\n     allocation and oversight of facility, fiscal, and personnel resources\n     within the college. Oversees faculty and staff personnel actions,\n     including evaluation, retention, promotion, tenure, and advocates for\n     competitive compensation to support the recruitment and retention of\n     high-quality personnel. Leads and participates in the college's strategic\n     planning and continuous improvement, including curriculum, teaching and\n     learning, scholarship, professional and fiscal development. Leads the development of internal and external\n     relationships for support of the college's teaching, scholarship, and strategic\n     growth through partnerships, donations, and grants. Represents the college at the University level and\n     coordinates effectively with other divisions of the University and performs other duties as assigned. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications An earned\ndoctorate in a discipline represented in or closely related to those\nrepresented in the college. Earned\ntenure and rank of full professor, or eligibility for promotion to full\nprofessor upon appointment consistent with the established promotion criteria\nin the unit and program of appointment. Demonstrated\nsuccess in higher education leadership and administration of an operational\nunit at the chair level or above, including oversight of budgets, personnel,\nand complex organizational operations. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strategic\nLeadership and Organizational Acumen Demonstrates\na comprehensive understanding of higher education, including academic affairs,\nenrollment trends, accreditation, shared governance, and the external\nenvironment affecting colleges and universities. Demonstrates strategic\nthinking and aligns college priorities, resources, and initiatives with the\nUniversity's mission and strategic plan. Actively seeks relevant information,\ndata, expertise, and perspectives to evaluate complex issues and make informed\ndecisions that advance long-term institutional goals. Academic\nLeadership and Professional Expertise Demonstrates\na record of achievement in teaching, scholarship, creative activity, and\nservice sufficient to earn the respect and confidence of faculty and academic\nleaders. Maintains current knowledge of emerging trends, best practices, and\ninnovations relevant to education, human sciences, and higher education.\nSupports academic excellence and student success through continuous improvement\nand evidence-based decision making. Operational\nand Resource Management Effectively\nmanages personnel, financial, physical, and technological resources to advance\nthe college's mission and strategic priorities. Demonstrates strong planning,\norganizational, and project management skills. Uses data and assessment results\nto evaluate opportunities, allocate resources, and achieve desired outcomes\nwhile maintaining accountability and operational effectiveness. Communication\nand Advocacy Communicates\nclearly, professionally, and effectively with diverse internal and external\nconstituencies. Demonstrates strong written, verbal, and interpersonal\ncommunication skills. Listens actively, fosters open dialogue, and promotes\ntransparency in decision making. Effectively advocates for the college, its\nfaculty, staff, students, and programs. Relationship\nBuilding and Collaboration Builds\nand sustains productive relationships with faculty, staff, students, alumni,\ncommunity partners, industry leaders, donors, and university leadership.\nDemonstrates the ability to foster collaboration across academic and\nadministrative units. Establishes credibility and trust through ethical\nleadership, integrity, and mutual respect. Leadership\nand Talent Development Provides\nvisionary, collaborative, and inclusive leadership. Creates an environment that\nsupports faculty and staff success through mentoring, professional development,\nsuccession planning, and recognition of achievement. Establishes clear\nexpectations, promotes accountability, manages change effectively, and inspires\na culture of excellence and continuous improvement. Preferred Qualifications Prior successful\nexperience working with various accreditation bodies (e.g., The Commission on\nColleges and Universities, CAEP, APA). Experience\nwith community partnerships, industry engagement, and alumni relations. Demonstrated\noversight of traditional, online, hybrid, or innovative academic programs. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
