    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5601?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Polymer Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Polymer Science and Engineering | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Polymer Science and Engineering Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5601 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Polymer Science and Engineering The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Polymer Science and Engineering. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Polymer Science and Engineering Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must be submitted online at https://usm.csod.com . A complete application will include: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Statement of research plans Brief statement of teaching philosophy that includes interest in specific core courses in the polymer science and engineering graduate and undergraduate curricula, particularly courses in polymer physics and polymer engineering Name and contact information for at least three references (letters will be requested following initial review). Review of applications will begin November 13, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the committee and/or hiring authority. For inquiries, contact Dr. Derek Patton, Director, School of Polymer Science and Engineering at derek.patton@usm.edu . Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Polymer Science and Engineering (SPSE) at The University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. We seek candidates whose research and teaching will complement and expand the School’s strengths in polymer science and engineering. We are particularly interested in candidates developing research programs broadly within polymer physics, physical polymer chemistry, or polymer engineering, with the disciplinary expertise to contribute to core undergraduate and graduate teaching in these areas. Outstanding candidates in other contemporary areas of polymer science and engineering are also encouraged to apply. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop and sustain an externally funded, internationally recognized research program. Deliver high-impact instruction in undergraduate and graduate courses in polymer science and engineering, fostering a dynamic and experiential learning environment. Mentor and supervise graduate and undergraduate researchers, emphasizing scholarly excellence and professional development. Contribute to the mission of the school, college, university, and broader scientific community through professional service. Perform other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Earned Ph.D. by the start date in polymer science and engineering or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated record of research productivity, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications, professional presentations, and/or grant submissions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Ability to work effectively, collaboratively, and collegially with students, staff, and faculty Commitment to fostering a world-class research and learning environment in which faculty, staff, and students can thrive Exceptional written and oral communication skills Knowledge associated with use and application of common instrumentation and methodologies in polymer science and engineering Preferred Qualifications Postdoctoral research experience with clear potential to build collaborative research programs within SPSE and across disciplines About the School: The School of Polymer Science and Engineering (SPSE) is one of the nation's few academic units devoted entirely to polymer science and engineering. SPSE comprises 13 faculty members, including multiple early-career awardees. Research in the School spans polymer composites and materials for extreme environments, including fire-retardant and carbon–carbon systems; biomaterials and polymers for human health, including tissue repair, regeneration, and therapeutic delivery; materials for energy and sustainability; optoelectronic materials; and advanced coatings. SPSE maintains a robust, well-funded research portfolio supported by federal agencies, industry, and private foundations. The Thames Polymer Science Research Center provides state-of-the-art facilities for polymer research, including NMR (400/600 MHz), TEM, SAXS/WAXS, XPS/UPS, polymer processing (extrusion/injection molding), composite fabrication, and advanced thermal, rheological, and mechanical characterization tools. SPSE sustains one of the largest polymer-focused graduate programs in the country alongside a growing ABET-accredited undergraduate program, and offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees in polymer science and engineering. For more information about SPSE, visit usm.edu/polymer-science-engineering . About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5600?c=usm": {
      "title": "Custodial Area Supervisor",
      "description": "Custodial Area Supervisor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Custodial Area Supervisor Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5600 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Custodial Area Supervisor The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Custodial Area Supervisor. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Residence Life Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 12.31 - 16.08 Pay Grade N03 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Works with the Custodial Supervisor to supervise, coordinate, provide leadership, developmnent of an effective team of custodial personnel, and participates in the care, cleaning, and general housekeeping of all Housing and Residence Life buildings.  Assist the custodial supervisor in ensuring that all assigned tasks are completed.  Uses proper methods and materials in cleaning and care for the assigned areas and equipment.  This position is considered essential personnel and will require storm duty and emergency call-out. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provides leadership\nand instruction to small groups of custodians by leading or directing custodial\nactivities during scheduled work periods by the supervisor. Conducts inspection of assigned areas to ensure completion of work assignments.  Works with employees to ensure that\n     assigned areas work orders and other complaints are completed in a timely\n     manner.  Ensures that the custodians\n     have the proper materials and supplies in the buildings to do the jobs\n     effectively.  Works with staff to\n     make changes in assigned areas schedules to ensure that areas are serviced\n     in a timely manner.  Carries out\n     responsibilities in a timely, fair and objective manner.  Acts\n     as team lead when the Custodial Supervisor is out. Discusses general custodial procedures with personnel of the assigned areas implements changes in procedures of chemicals and supplies. Maintains knowledge of materials and supplies used in cleaning buildings. Must be able to show knowledge of and train employees on equipment commonly used in residence hall cleaning.  Examples include:  auto scrubbers, wet vacuum, carpet extraction, pressure washers, etc. Helps the custodial\n     supervisor and lead person when responding to emergency situations during\n     and after hours.  Emergency\n     situations may include; property damage, personal injury, flooding, water\n     leaks, overflowing restroom fixtures, broken windows/door glass, and\n     accidents resulting in the appearance of bodily fluids (blood, vomit,\n     waste and urine). Makes work assignments in accordance with predetermined schedules, reviews the work of employees and assists in training of new personnel. Trains, organizes, schedules and assigns work routines to a large group of employees. Works from oral and written instruction to make immediate changes in the work program to meet modification of services desired and performs other duties as assigned. Receives and disposes of variety of complaints and expedites for service. Sweep, mop and scrub floors; dust and clean surfaces;\nwashes windows, walls, blinds, trash cans, air conditioning grills/vents and\nglass doors.  Cleans rooms, replenishes\nsupplies and cleans drinking fountains. \nCleans and polishes as needed. \nAssists with taking out trash, compacting dumpsters, etc.  Makes sure the entrances and exits of the\nassigned areas are clean.  Clean other\nareas as assigned Minimum Qualifications One year certificate from college or technical school; or 3 years related experience and/or training; or equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of University policies and procedures, professional standards and regulations, safety requirements and a knowledge of basic first aid. Knowledge of cleaning techniques and procedures, and the use of custodial materials, tools, equipment, and chemicals. Skill in managing ones’ own time and the time of others while monitoring/assessing the performance of self, other individuals, or organizations to make improvements or take corrective action. Skill in the operation of office equipment including, but not limited to, multiline telephone, typewriter, calculator, multi-function printer/copy/scan/fax machine and computer as well as computer applications including spreadsheet, database, and word processing software. Ability to handle difficult and stressful situations with professional composure and the ability to react and respond quickly and calmly in emergency situations. Ability to establish and maintain a good rapport with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to work successfully as a member of a team and independently with moderate supervision. Skill in material resources management through obtaining and seeing to the appropriate use of equipment, facilities, and materials needed to do certain work. Ability to obtain a driver’s license prior to employment. Ability to work evenings, nights, and weekends as necessary. Ability to process and handle confidential information with discretion. Preferred Qualifications Prefer 4 years of work experience in similar or related field of work, familiarity with computer based time clock and familiarity with maintenance work order systems. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5597?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Jazz Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Jazz Studies | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Jazz Studies Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5597 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Jazz Studies The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music and Director of Jazz Studies. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Music Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date December 1, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Required Documents: Cover letter addressing the candidate’s qualifications, experience, vision for leading a contemporary collegiate Jazz Studies program, and potential to contribute to a modern music curriculum Curriculum vitae Contact information for four professional references Video recordings of rehearsals and/or ensemble instruction Video or audio recordings of performances (Please submit all audio or video via YouTube or Vimeo links in a Word file or PDF) Supporting Materials: Additional materials may be requested at a later date. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Music at the University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for the position of Director of Jazz Studies . This nine-month, tenure-track position will begin in August 2027. The Southern Miss School of Music enjoys a longstanding national and international reputation for musical excellence. Its accredited programs provide opportunities for musical and professional growth at the undergraduate through the doctoral levels. Our diverse student body works with distinguished faculty members who perform on world-class stages and bring their rich experiences to our Hattiesburg campus every day. Ensembles include the Southern Chorale, Symphony Orchestra, Wind Ensemble, Symphonic Winds, Pride of Mississippi Marching Band, Southern Opera and Musical Theatre, Jazz Lab Bands, and numerous outstanding studio ensembles. Students regularly perform at regional, national, and international events, attend master classes with internationally known guest artists, and become award-winning teachers, performers, and creators around the globe. The Jazz Studies program has been in existence for over 50 years. Its ensembles include two big bands and several diverse combos, including the award-winning Southern Miss Jazztet. It has hosted many outstanding artists including Gregory Tardy, Joel Frahm, The KC Chamber Jazz Quintet, and the Amina Figarova Jazz Sextet. Notable guest artists who have performed with Jazz Lab Band 1 include Ellis Marsalis, Jeff Coffin, Jovino Santos Neto, John Fedchock, Carl Allen, and Mike Clark. We seek a dynamic musician, educator, and program builder with a forward-looking vision for jazz education and a demonstrated commitment to preparing students for an evolving professional music landscape. The successful candidate will provide artistic, curricular, and administrative leadership for the Jazz Studies program and will play a central role in its continued growth and development. The Director of Jazz Studies will lead an active and visible program that honors the traditions and history of jazz while embracing contemporary practices, emerging technologies, interdisciplinary collaboration, entrepreneurship, and the diverse ways musicians build sustainable careers in the twenty-first century. Recruitment and program growth will be a significant priority of this position. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active recruitment strategy; cultivate relationships with prospective students, school music programs, community colleges, professional musicians, alumni, and other partners; and establish a strong regional and national presence for the Jazz Studies program. The program includes large and small ensembles as well as courses in performance, improvisation, theory, arranging, and history. Jazz ensembles and most core jazz courses are open to all majors, so the director works with students from both the School of Music and broader university. Professionally, the Director of Jazz Studies will maintain an active record of creative activity as a performer, composer, arranger, or some combination of these. That record should reach regional, national, and international audiences, consistent with the tenure and promotion expectations of a comprehensive school of music at a Carnegie R1 research institution. This full-time, nine-month, tenure-track appointment comes at the rank of Assistant Professor. For full consideration, applications must be submitted by November 16, 2026 . Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Joseph E. Jones (joseph.e.jones@usm.edu). Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provide artistic and administrative leadership for the Jazz Studies program, including developing a clear vision for its continued growth and distinction Direct jazz ensembles and jazz combos as assigned, maintaining a high standard of performance Create meaningful performance opportunities on and off campus for students and increase the regional and national visibility of the Jazz Studies program Teach courses in jazz appropriate to the candidate’s expertise and the needs of the school Develop and implement a comprehensive recruitment strategy, including regular engagement with prospective students, school programs, community colleges, festivals, conferences, guest artists, and other recruitment opportunities Encourage innovative programming and creative projects that reflect both traditions in jazz and innovations in contemporary music Collaborate with other school and academic disciplines, professional musicians, arts organizations, and community partners Cultivate guest artist residencies, festivals, clinics, touring opportunities, recording projects, and other initiatives that enhance the student experience and profile of the program Teach, mentor, and advise graduate students in jazz, developing appropriate curricula related to the area Oversee management of scholarship and operating budgets for the area Coordinate with administration the teaching assignments of adjunct faculty and graduate assistants Maintain an active professional profile as a performer, educator, scholar, composer/arranger, producer, or other creative practitioner Foster an inclusive and collaborative culture that supports artistic excellence as well as student achievement, retention, and professional development Participate in school, college, university service as appropriate Minimum Qualification DMA in jazz studies, music performance, or a closely related field Demonstrated record of excellence as a jazz performer, educator, conductor/director, composer/arranger, or other jazz professional Demonstrated experience directing jazz ensembles and/or coaching small ensembles Evidence of successful teaching at the collegiate, secondary, or comparable professional level Demonstrated knowledge of jazz history, repertoire, performance practices, and pedagogy Evidence of or potential to recruit, mentor, and retain students Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with faculty, students, administrators, professional musicians, and community partners Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Familiarity with (or ability to learn) Canvas, the university’s online learning management systems (LMS). Familiarity with (or ability to learn) Microsoft Office, including Outlook and Teams. Familiarity with university-level recruitment and/or retention strategies. Preferred Qualifications Successful assistance in recruiting students and building or growing a collegiate jazz program Experience developing innovative curricula or programs that respond to changes in the professional music industry Evidence of successful interdisciplinary collaborations and/or partnerships with professional and community organizations Experience incorporating contemporary commercial music, popular music, global influences, or other complementary styles and practices within a jazz curriculum Professional profile as a performer, educator, conductor, composer/arranger, producer, or creative artist Collegiate teaching and ensemble-directing experience Experience teaching or mentoring students in music entrepreneurship, career development, audience development, marketing, branding, project management, or other aspects of professional musicianship Experience with participating in festivals, guest artist programs, tours, recordings, community engagement initiatives, or other high-impact projects Skills and/or experience with fundraising, grant writing, donor cultivation, or development of external partnerships Budget management skills and/or experience About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5594?c=usm": {
      "title": "Registration Specialist",
      "description": "Registration Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Registration Specialist Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5594 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Registration Specialist The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Registration Specialist. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Office of the University Registrar Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N02 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Reporting to the Supervisor for Registration and Student Relations, the primary duty of this position is to process the assignment of\nclassroom space for approved academic and non-academic requests.  Respond to inquiries concerning course\nscheduling and registration issues.  Serve\nas a back-up in the absence of the Supervisor for Registration and Student\nRelations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Coordinates the\n     assignment of University classrooms for academic and non-academic\n     requests. Serves as primary point\n     of contact for academic departments requesting classroom space. Processes\n     classroom and event information into the University space utilization\n     software. Assist students, faculty,\n     and staff with course scheduling and registration issues. Assist the campus\n     community during the academic units schedule entry period. Performs other duties as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree(GED). One to three months related experience and/or training or equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge,\nSkills, and Abilities (KSA) Working knowledge of PeopleSoft. Excellent communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to work with multiple departments across campus. Strong analytical and problem solving skills. Proficient with Microsoft Excel and ability to use Microsoft Word. Preferred Qualifications One to two years experience employed in a higher education environment. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
