    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5577?c=usm": {
      "title": "Marine Technician III (Cal Lab)",
      "description": "Marine Technician III (Cal Lab) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Marine Technician III (Cal Lab) Gulfport, MS, United States | req5577 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/5/2026 Back to Search Marine Technician III (Cal Lab) The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Marine Technician III (Cal Lab). Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Pay Grade E12 Posting Close Date October 16, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Marine\nTechnician III performs calibration, testing, and evaluation of marine\ninstrumentation to ensure the accuracy and precision of measurement systems.\nThis position utilizes various measurement and testing equipment in a\ncalibration laboratory setting and performs calibration procedures in\naccordance with established standards, protocols, and regulatory requirements.\nThe Marine Technician III maintains calibration documentation, troubleshoots\nequipment performance issues, and performs necessary adjustments or repairs to\nensure equipment accuracy and reliability. This position also and support\ncalibration operations. collaborates with multidisciplinary teams to evaluate\nsystem performance. Primary\nJob Duties and Responsibilities Develop and keep current all calibration procedures for the newly established USM Calibration Laboratory. Serve as technical expert on calibration requirements for oceanographic sensors and set protocols for all calibration activities. Establish calibration procedures specific to available equipment and future requirements. Lead efforts to establish ISO/IEC 17025 accreditation and assure quality processes align with international standards, including International Organization for Standardization/International Electrotechnical Commission (ISO/IEC) 17025 and National Institute of Standards and Technology (NIST) requirements. Independently determine corrective actions for more complex calibration issues. Accurately records calibration results and maintains detailed records, reports, and supporting documentation related to calibration activities. Troubleshoots and diagnoses equipment malfunctions, performance issues, and measurement inaccuracies identified during calibration and testing processes. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in Marine Science, Engineering or\nElectronics Technology or a related field. Two to four (2-4) years of\nexperience working with oceanographic sensors, instrumentation, or equipment. Must\nbe willing to travel for training at vendor locations.  Must be a U.S Citizen and have a valid\ndriver’s license. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of equipment testing, calibration, and troubleshooting procedures. Ability to collect, organize, and maintain data related to oceanographic sensor and equipment performance and calibration readiness. Ability to prepare and maintain accurate calibration records, reports, and supporting documentation. Knowledge of basic International Organization for Standardization (ISO) procedures and requirements. Ability to support internal and external audits by maintaining complete, accurate, and audit-ready documentation and supporting evidence. Ability to identify equipment performance issues and assist with appropriate adjustments, repairs, or corrective actions. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow established calibration procedures, technical specifications, and quality requirements. Ability to attend and successfully complete training specific to calibration equipment operations and procedures. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s\ndegree in Engineering discipline. Five (5) or more years’ experience working in\na calibration laboratory setting. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5599?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Director - Finance and Administrative Operations",
      "description": "Assistant Director - Finance and Administrative Operations | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Director - Finance and Administrative Operations Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5599 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Director - Finance and Administrative Operations The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Director - Finance and Administrative Operations. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division College of Nursing and Health Professions Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N07 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please contact the School Director, Dr. Melissa Kossman (melissa.k.kossman@usm.edu), with any questions. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Assistant Director – Finance and\nAdministrative Operations provides administrative, financial, and operational\nsupport for the School of Health Professions. This position coordinates\nacademic and personnel administrative processes, purchasing and financial\ndocumentation, records management, events, communications, and facility and\ninventory activities. The Assistant Director – Finance and Administrative\nOperations serves as a primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff,\nadministrators, and external stakeholders and supports accreditation,\ncompliance, and reporting activities. This position also supervises student\nworkers and assists with maintaining efficient day-to-day operations of the\nSchool. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provides administrative support for the School of Health Professions and serves as a primary point of contact for students, faculty, staff, administrators, visitors, and external stakeholders. Responds to inquiries, manages shared email accounts and calendars, maintains office records, coordinates communications, and directs individuals to appropriate University resources. Coordinates and supports academic administrative processes, including course scheduling, textbook adoption, faculty workload documentation, syllabus collection and review, student enrollment coordination, and maintenance of academic and program records. Uses University systems, including SOAR, SOARFin, SOARHR, and Canvas, to enter, retrieve, verify, and maintain information. Supports faculty and staff recruitment, onboarding, and personnel administration by coordinating interviews, preparing materials, processing required documentation, maintaining credential and personnel records, and completing documentation for adjunct faculty, student workers, guest speakers, standardized patients, and other temporary or contracted personnel. The existing description assigns these recruitment and personnel responsibilities to the position. Processes and tracks purchases, reconciles PCard transactions, maintains supporting financial documentation, processes travel and reimbursement documentation, and prepares budget-related records and financial reports. Monitors purchasing and reimbursement activities for compliance with University procedures and applicable funding requirements. Coordinates meetings, interviews, orientations, ceremonies, trainings, student presentations, and other School events, including scheduling, room arrangements, technology, catering, purchasing, and logistical support. Prepares, edits, proofreads, formats, and distributes correspondence, reports, agendas, meeting minutes, forms, announcements, and other School communications. Supports accreditation, assessment, compliance, audit, and institutional reporting activities by collecting, organizing, verifying, maintaining, and submitting required records and documentation. Coordinates with appropriate University offices to obtain information and assists with ensuring administrative processes are completed according to established requirements and deadlines. Serves as a School point of contact for facilities and inventory matters. Maintains and tracks inventory, assists with required inventory audits, coordinates equipment and laboratory maintenance, orders operational and instructional supplies, submits and tracks maintenance work orders, and serves as a liaison with Physical Plant and other University offices. These responsibilities are currently spread across several individual tasks. Supervises student workers, assists with interviews, develops work schedules, assigns and monitors work, and provides guidance and training. Performs other duties as\nassigned. Minimum Qualifications Associate’s degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in Business Administration, Office Administration, Healthcare\nAdministration, Management, Accounting, Finance, or a related field. Two (2)\nyears of experience in administrative support, office operations, financial\nadministration, or a related area. In lieu of an associate degree, applicants\ncan meet minimum qualifications by demonstrating a High School Diploma or\nGeneral Education Diploma (GED) and at least five (5) years of experience in\nadministrative support, office operations, financial administration, or a\nrelated area. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of administrative and office management practices and procedures. Knowledge of purchasing, financial documentation, recordkeeping, and reconciliation processes. Knowledge of Microsoft Office, including Word, Excel, Outlook, and Teams. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple responsibilities and meet established deadlines. Ability to maintain accurate administrative, financial, academic, and personnel records. Ability to maintain confidentiality and appropriately handle sensitive information. Ability to communicate effectively with students, faculty, staff, administrators, vendors, and the public. Ability to interpret and follow established University policies, procedures, and administrative requirements. Skill in preparing and proofreading correspondence, reports, meeting minutes, forms, and other professional documents. Skill in data entry, spreadsheet maintenance, records management, and administrative systems. Ability to work independently and collaboratively\nwhile responding to changing operational priorities. Preferred Qualifications One (1) year of experience providing\nadministrative support in higher education, healthcare, health professions\neducation, or a related setting. One (1) year of experience with academic\nadministration, student records, course scheduling, purchasing, travel, or\nfinancial processes. One (1) year of experience supporting accreditation,\nassessment, compliance, or institutional reporting activities. Three (3) years\nof experience preparing professional correspondence, reports, meeting minutes,\nand other administrative documents. One (1) or more year(s) of experience using\nuniversity administrative systems or comparable enterprise systems. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5598?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of French",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor of French | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Teaching Professor of French Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5598 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Teaching Professor of French The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor of French. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Social Sciences and Global Studies Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit a cover letter, C.V., teaching\nevaluations or other evidence of teaching effectiveness, statement of teaching\nphilosophy, and contact information for three professional references. Review\nof applications will begin November 6 and will continue until position is\nfilled. For further questions about the position, please contact Dr. Katie\nAngus via email at katie.angus@usm.edu or phone at 601-266-5325. Application materials must be submitted online at https://jobs.usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity is unable to sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Social Science and Global Studies at The University of Southern\nMississippi invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track, Assistant\nTeaching Professor of French beginning August 2027; this is a teaching-track\nposition with opportunities for promotion. The School is seeking French\ngeneralist candidates who will demonstrate a strong commitment to undergraduate\nand graduate education, teach a full range of undergraduate and graduate courses\nin both the World Languages BA and the Master of Arts in the Teaching of\nLanguages programs, advise and mentor students, serve on committees, and work\nwith graduate teaching assistants to implement standards-based practices. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach\n     four courses per semester, fall and spring, face-to-face and online as\n     needed. Hold\n     regular office hours. Mentor\n     and advise students in the program. Attend\n     faculty meetings as determined by the Director of the School of Social\n     Science and Global Studies and program meetings as determined by the\n     program coordinators. Engage\n     in professional development and/or scholarly activities appropriate to the\n     mission of the School, College, and University. Provide\n     service to assist the functioning of the School, College, and University. Perform\n     other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. with specialization in Frenc h , second language acquisition , teacher education , or related field , with at least 18 hours of graduate French , completed by August 2027 . Native or near-native proficiency in Frenc h . Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Knowledge\n     of second language acquisition, French language pedagogy, and\n     standards-based approaches to language teaching. Ability\n     to articulate concepts, course content, and instructions clearly and\n     effectively to students across undergraduate and graduate levels and in\n     face-to-face and online environments. Capacity\n     to build positive, respectful, and professional relationships with\n     students, colleagues, graduate teaching assistants, and other university\n     personnel. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching and mentoring in a university setting with a diverse student body. Online teaching and online course design experience. Graduate level teaching experience. Interest in leading study abroad programs . About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5591?c=usm": {
      "title": "Instructor of Architectural Engineering Technology",
      "description": "Instructor of Architectural Engineering Technology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor of Architectural Engineering Technology Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5591 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/2/2026 Back to Search Instructor of Architectural Engineering Technology The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Instructor of Architectural Engineering Technology. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Construction and Design Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 65,000.00 - 65,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special\nInstructions to Applicants Please include a Cover Letter indicating how the\ncandidate's background and credentials meet the position's responsibilities and\nqualifications, a current Curriculum Vitae, a statement of Teaching Philosophy\n(maximum 2 pages), unofficial transcripts for undergraduate and graduate\ncoursework completed, and a list of names and contact information for three\nprofessional references. Submission of a studio portfolio is encouraged. To receive full consideration, applicants should submit all application\nmaterials by November 16, 2026. Review of applications will begin\nthereafter and continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a\nfull-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not\nsponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job\nSummary The School of Construction and Design at The\nUniversity of Southern Mississippi invites applications for a full-time,\n9-month, non-tenure-track faculty position in Architectural Engineering\nTechnology at the Instructor level, with a target start date of August 2027.\nThis is an on-site position based on the Hattiesburg campus, with primary\nresponsibilities involving face-to-face instruction and in-person engagement\nwith students, faculty, and the School community. Primary\nDuties and Responsibilities Teach a\n     full load of undergraduate courses each semester (studio and lecture). Utilize\n     effective teaching methods to ensure that all course outcomes are met. Support\n     the Architectural Engineering Technology program including new course\n     development and curriculum improvement. Maintain\n     regular office hours. Fulfill\n     institutional service duties within the School, College, University, and\n     community. Engage\n     in student-related activities such as supervising student projects, advising\n     student organizations, and coaching student teams for competitions. Provide\n     end of the semester course assessment data. Build\n     and maintain strong relationships with industry partners. Perform\n     other duties as assigned. Minimum\nQualifications A professional Bachelor of Architecture\n(B.Arch.) degree or a master’s degree in architecture or a closely related\nfield. At least one degree in architecture. Demonstrated commitment to diversity, equity, and inclusion. Commitment to collegiality and evidence of effective communication skills. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Working\n     knowledge of design, modeling, and rendering software, such as AutoCAD,\n     Revit, SketchUp, or similar platforms. Ability\n     to integrate current and emerging technologies into teaching and student\n     learning. Preferred Qualifications Previous teaching experience at the collegiate level. Professional registration or licensure. Significant professional or industry experience. Working knowledge of emerging digital technologies and AI-assisted tools\napplicable to architectural design, visualization, documentation, and/or\neducation. Demonstrated commitment to innovative teaching, student success, continuous\nimprovement, and service to the program. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5596?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music Education | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Music Education Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5596 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Music Education The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Education. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Music Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date December 1, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Required Documents: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae that includes a list of courses taught Contact information for three references Research agenda statement Teaching philosophy statement Supporting Materials: Additional materials may be requested at a later date. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Music at the University of Southern Mississippi is now accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Education . This nine-month, tenure-track position will begin in August 2027. The University of Southern Mississippi, founded in 1910, is a public Carnegie R1 research university with its main campus in Hattiesburg and a coastal campus in Long Beach. It has been accredited by the National Association of Schools of Music since 1938. The School of Music offers the B.A., B.M., and B.M.Ed. degrees, the M.M. and M.M.E., and the D.M.A. in performance and pedagogy and in conducting. Students perform in ensembles that include the USM Symphony Orchestra, the Wind Ensemble, the Southern Chorale, the Southern Opera and Musical Theatre Company, and The Pride of Mississippi Marching Band. More than 40 full-time faculty perform, present, and publish nationally and internationally and bring that work into the studio and classroom. The School enrolls students from a wide range of backgrounds, from across Mississippi and around the world. For full consideration, applications must be submitted by November 13, 2026 . Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Joseph E. Jones (joseph.e.jones@usm.edu). Primary Duties and Responsibilities This faculty member will teach both undergraduate and graduate music education courses as well as conduct research that contributes to the field. Additional responsibilities may include, but are not limited to, supervising student teachers, supervising graduate student research, engaging in professional activities and service to the School, community, and profession, and participating in the planning and implementation of School business. Minimum Qualification Ph.D. or equivalent in Music Education by the time of appointment. Minimum of three years of K-12 music teaching experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Familiarity\n     with (or ability to learn) Canvas, the university’s online learning\n     management systems (LMS). Familiarity\n     with (or ability to learn) Microsoft Office, including Outlook and Teams. Familiarity\n     with university-level recruitment and/or retention strategies. Preferred Qualifications Five or more years of K-12 music teaching experience, especially in elementary/general. Training or certification in elementary/general music pedagogies (e.g., Orff Schulwerk, Kodály, Dalcroze, Modern Band, world drumming, or similar approaches). Evidence of successful instruction of undergraduate and/or graduate music education courses. Evidence of successful research activity in the field. Record of both in-person and online teaching. Brass or woodwind teaching experience. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5595?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Theory",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Music Theory | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor of Music Theory Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5595 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor of Music Theory The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Theory. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Music Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date December 1, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Required Documents: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae that includes a list of courses taught Contact information for three references Supporting Materials: Additional materials may be requested at a later date. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Music at the University of Southern Mississippi is now accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor of Music Theory . Area of specialization is open. This nine-month, tenure-track position will begin in August 2027. The University of Southern Mississippi, founded in 1910, is a public Carnegie R1 research university with its main campus in Hattiesburg and a coastal campus in Long Beach. It has been accredited by the National Association of Schools of Music since 1938. The School of Music offers the B.A., B.M., and B.M.Ed. degrees, the M.M. and M.M.E., and the D.M.A. in performance and pedagogy and in conducting. Students perform in ensembles that include the USM Symphony Orchestra, the Wind Ensemble, the Southern Chorale, the Southern Opera and Musical Theatre Company, and The Pride of Mississippi Marching Band. More than 40 full-time faculty perform, present, and publish nationally and internationally and bring that work into the studio and classroom. The School enrolls students from a wide range of backgrounds, from across Mississippi and around the world. For full consideration, applications must be submitted by November 16, 2026 . Questions may be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Joseph E. Jones (joseph.e.jones@usm.edu). Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaching expectations – Music theory faculty typically teach six courses per year, three per semester, and serve on graduate student committees. The School offers courses ranging from undergraduate theory and ear training to graduate-level seminars. Research expectations – Faculty develop a clear research agenda with a growing record of peer-reviewed conference presentations and publications. Service expectations – Faculty engage in service activities within the School of Music, particularly graduate project advising, and across the university. Faculty are also encouraged to serve or otherwise participate in their professional organizations. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in music theory by the time of appointment University teaching experience as instructor of record Evidence of (or potential for) scholarly achievement in the field of music theory Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Familiarity with (or ability to learn) Canvas, the university’s online learning management systems (LMS). Familiarity with (or ability to learn) Microsoft Office, including Outlook and Teams. Familiarity with university-level recruitment and/or retention strategies. Preferred Qualifications Experience mentoring or advising graduate student research Experience teaching undergraduate music theory and ear training sequences Experience teaching graduate-level courses About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5593?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5593 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor of Philosophy. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Philosophy and Religion Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date January 3, 2027 Special\nInstructions to Applicants To\napply, upload a letter of application, curriculum vitae, graduate transcripts,\nnames and email addresses of three references, teaching portfolio, and an\narticle/chapter length writing sample.  All attachments must be\nuploaded at the time of submission. In addition, please send three confidential\nletters of recommendation directly to usmphilosophysearch27@groups.usm.edu.\nPlease apply by December 1, 2026 to receive full consideration. Questions\nshould be directed to Dr. Brian LaPierre, Director, School of Humanities, 118\nCollege Drive #5037, The University of Southern Mississippi, Hattiesburg,\nMS  39406-0001; Email: Brian.LaPierre@usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a\nfull-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not\nsponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job\nSummary The Philosophy & Religion program in the School of Humanities at the\nUniversity of Southern Mississippi invites qualified applicants for a\nfull-time, 9-month, non-tenure track, Assistant Teaching Professor in\nPhilosophy to begin Fall 2027. The program has a new inter-disciplinary BA in\nPhilosophy, Religion, and Law that offers three pathways of concentration:\nEthics, Philosophy of Law, and Religion and World Cultures. We are seeking a\ncandidate whose area of specialization is open, but we are looking for someone\nto fulfill our needs in applied ethics, particularly Environmental Ethics and\nHealthcare Ethics. In addition, the program would like to develop and offer a\nnew course in Ethics and Artificial Intelligence. The teaching load is 4/4. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach\n     undergraduate courses in Environmental Ethics, Healthcare Ethics, possibly\n     Ethics and Artificial Intelligence (this would be a new course offering),\n     and survey courses in both conventional and online formats Advise\n     and mentor undergraduate students Participate\n     in program assessment Fulfill\n     service obligations appropriate to teaching-track faculty Performs\n     other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications PhD in Philosophy by the time of appointment Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of computers and appropriate teaching technologies Preferred Qualifications A record of publication and scholarship as well as teaching experience in both conventional and online formats. Knowledge of Canvas helpful. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5585?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5585 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Procurement and Contract Services Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 70,536.00 - 95,432.00 Pay Grade E14 Posting Close Date October 24, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Assistant Director of Procurement & Contract Services provides leadership and oversight for the procurement of goods and services on behalf of The University of Southern Mississippi. This position performs complex professional and administrative work involving formal and informal purchasing, solicitation development, contract review and negotiation, scope of work development, purchasing card administration, and procurement documentation. The Assistant Director coordinates day-to-day purchasing activities and ensures procurement processes comply with applicable University, Institutions of Higher Learning (IHL), and State of Mississippi policies, procedures, and purchasing requirements. This position serves as an authorized purchasing agent with designated authority to obligate the University for the acquisition of goods and services and assists in coordinating the University’s contract management process. The position supervises procurement personnel and exercises considerable independent judgment in evaluating purchasing needs, resolving complex procurement matters, and supporting effective University-wide procurement operations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Directs and coordinates day-to-day procurement activities for the University, including formal and informal purchasing processes, and ensures the acquisition of goods and services complies with applicable University, IHL, State of Mississippi, and other applicable procurement requirements. Supervises and provides guidance to buyers, purchasing card personnel, and other assigned procurement staff; establishes work priorities, reviews work for accuracy and compliance, provides coaching and professional development, and supports required state purchasing certifications. Evaluates complex and\nnonstandard purchasing requests, determines appropriate procurement methods,\nand reviews or recommends contract and procurement awards in coordination with\nUniversity departments. Maintains applicable University purchasing and\ntechnology procedures and identifies opportunities to improve procurement\nprocesses and operational efficiency. Coordinates formal solicitations and competitive procurement activities, including bids and Requests for Proposals (RFPs); prepares and maintains specifications, legal advertisements, bid documentation, tabulations, vendor notifications, addenda, bid bonds, and other required procurement records; and utilizes applicable State of Mississippi procurement systems to support solicitation and purchasing approval processes. Reviews and assists with negotiating procurement contracts; develops scopes of work and other procurement documentation; investigates contract-related concerns; coordinates with the Office of General Counsel as appropriate; and prepares contracts and supporting documentation for review, approval, and execution. Coordinates the University’s contract management process, including contract intake, review coordination, negotiations, execution workflows, compliance monitoring, records management, and communication with University departments. Develops and provides training and guidance to faculty and staff regarding purchasing, contracting, and contract submission processes. Assists with the administration and oversight of the University’s purchasing card program, including review of purchasing activities and implementation of procedures designed to support compliance with applicable State of Mississippi, IHL, and University requirements. Evaluates opportunities to improve purchasing methods and purchasing card utilization within applicable requirements. Serves as a procurement liaison for the Hattiesburg campus, Gulf Park, Gulf Coast Research Laboratory, and other University locations to promote consistent procurement practices, provide guidance to University departments, and support compliance with applicable purchasing requirements. Performs other duties as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in Business, Supply Chain\nManagement, or a related field; or eight (8) years of experience involving the\nacquisition of equipment, supplies, commodities, or services, including\ncontract review within a purchasing or procurement program; or an equivalent\ncombination of education and related experience. Advanced education may\nsubstitute for experience on a year-for-year basis. Must obtain Certified\nMississippi Purchasing Agent (CMPA) certification within the first year of\nemployment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of public procurement principles, practices, methods, and applicable purchasing requirements. Knowledge of contract administration, including drafting, reviewing, interpreting, and negotiating commercial contract terms, conditions, specifications, and scopes of work. Knowledge of competitive procurement processes and the evaluation of bids, proposals, quotations, and contract award recommendations. Skill in analyzing procurement, financial, technical, and contractual information and applying appropriate judgment to complex purchasing decisions. Skill in written and verbal communication, including communicating procurement requirements and providing clear guidance and training to University departments and external parties. Skill in using procurement technology, data management systems, and related applications to collect, organize, analyze, maintain, and present purchasing and contract information. Ability to identify and resolve complex procurement and contract-related issues while ensuring accuracy and compliance with established requirements. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple procurement activities, contracts, projects, and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to lead, supervise, delegate, and evaluate the work of assigned personnel while establishing effective working relationships with University departments, vendors, regulatory entities, and other stakeholders. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in Business, Supply Chain Management, or a related field. Eight (8)\nyears of professional-level experience in higher education or governmental\nprocurement. Extensive knowledge of State of Mississippi purchasing laws and\nexperience with State purchasing systems or current Certified Mississippi\nPurchasing Agent (CMPA) certification is preferred. Professional certification\nas a Certified Purchasing Manager (C.P.M.), Certified Professional in Supply\nManagement (CPSM), Certified Professional Public Buyer (CPPB), Certified Public\nPurchasing Officer (CPPO), or another nationally recognized procurement or\nsupply chain certification is also preferred. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5583?c=usm": {
      "title": "Utility and Refuse Crewman -Part Time",
      "description": "Utility and Refuse Crewman -Part Time | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Utility and Refuse Crewman -Part Time Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5583 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/1/2026 Back to Search Utility and Refuse Crewman -Part Time The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Utility and Refuse Crewman -Part Time. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Administration Physical Plant Position Type Staff Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 12.00 - 12.00 Pay Grade N02 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Collects and removes waste materials, refuse and recycling from all areas of the campus. Participates in trash removal services and general maintenance needs for assigned events, completing all tasks including football, baseball, work orders, etc. as assigned. This role also includes pickup and delivery of supplies and equipment to designated academic and athletic facilities, performing maintenance and restorative floor care, and conducting soft wash and/or pressure washing of building entrances and sidewalks. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Collects and disposes of refuse from campus and assists Office of Sustainability with recycling collection as coordinated with the Manager of Sustainable Operations. Assists in the setup and removal of waste and recycling receptacles for large public areas and campus events, ensuring these spaces are clean before and after use. Maintains the cleanliness and upkeep of university facilities and grounds by utilizing cleaning equipment (blowers, pressure washers), performing floor care (scrubbing, buffing, vacuuming, shampooing), and ensuring the sanitation of waste disposal areas (dumpsters, bins) and surrounding environments, including odor control. Also assists with cleaning coverage in academic and athletic facilities as directed. Transports and distributes necessary supplies and equipment to designated university buildings in a timely and accurate manner. Responds to emergency situations during and after hours. Emergency situations may include property damage, personal injury, water leaks, flooding, overflowing restroom fixtures, broken window or door glass, and accidents resulting in the appearance of bodily fluids (blood, vomit waste, and urine). Serves as a member of the Physical Plant Essential Personnel and as directed by the Physical Plant participates in pre-emergency preparations and post emergency recovery efforts. Performs additional duties as assigned by Custodial Leadership. Minimum Qualifications Valid Driver’s License and the ability to obtain a driver’s clearance to operate university vehicles; six months of related experience and/or training. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exhibits strong active listening skills, characterized by attentiveness, patience, and the ability to understand and respond appropriately without interrupting. Proficient in the safe operation of various equipment including forklifts, University vehicles, carts, trailers, and standard hand tools (hammers, screwdrivers, pliers). Ability to establish and maintain a good rapport with university faculty and staff, students, and the general public. Ability to work successfully as a member of a team and independently with moderate supervision. Ability to understand and follow instructions. Ability to work evenings, nights, and weekends as necessary. Ability to respond quickly to emergencies. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, University policies and procedures. Preferred Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree (GED). Three (3) months of related experience in a higher education setting or commercial cleaning environment. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
