    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5590?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Director of Communications",
      "description": "Assistant Athletic Director of Communications | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Athletic Director of Communications Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5590 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/28/2026 Back to Search Assistant Athletic Director of Communications The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Athletic Director of Communications. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Sports Information Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade E09 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The\nAssistant Athletic Director for Communications plays a key leadership role\nwithin Southern Miss Athletics Communications and assists in developing and\nexecuting the department’s overall communications, storytelling, and social\nmedia strategy. This position serves as the primary communications contact for\nSouthern Miss Men’s Basketball and other assigned sports while providing\nstrategic communications support across the department’s Division I athletics\nprograms. The position works closely with coaches, student-athletes, athletics\nleadership, creative services, marketing, and other external units to\nstrengthen the Southern Miss brand, increase media exposure, and engage fans\nacross traditional, digital, and social platforms. The Assistant Athletic Director\nalso assists with the day-to-day management of Athletics Communications,\nincluding staff development, content planning, media relations, website\nmanagement, and communications strategy. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Assist in the development and execution of a comprehensive communications strategy for Southern Miss Athletics, including proactive storytelling, earned media, brand visibility, and consistent messaging across the department. Serve as the primary communications contact for Southern Miss Men's Basketball and other assigned sports, coordinating media relations and operations, interview requests, press conferences, credentials, statistics, game-day communications, and pre- and postgame media availability. Assist with the daily management of Athletics Communications and provide leadership, direction, and professional development for communications staff, graduate assistants, interns, and student workers. Develop and maintain relationships with local, regional, and national media while identifying opportunities to generate coverage and producing stories, press releases, features, announcements, and other communications highlighting Southern Miss teams, coaches, student-athletes, and departmental initiatives. Collaborate with creative services, marketing, photography, and other external units to develop and execute digital and social media strategies and ensure appropriate coverage that increases engagement, strengthens the Southern Miss brand, and expands the reach of athletics content. Assist with the strategic management and daily maintenance of SouthernMiss.com, ensuring accurate, timely, and engaging content across sport and departmental pages. Stay current on emerging communications platforms, technologies, media trends, and industry best practices and identify opportunities to enhance the visibility and storytelling capabilities of Southern Miss Athletics. Perform other duties and communications responsibilities as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s\ndegree from four-year college or university in business, marketing, sport\nmanagement, or other related field. Two to three years’ experience in an\nathletic department or other related field; or equivalent combination of\neducation and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of intercollegiate athletics communications, media relations, public relations, marketing, and strategic communications principles and practices. Ability to develop, implement, and evaluate comprehensive communications strategies that promote the visibility, reputation, and success of the Athletics Department. Ability to effectively communicate and tell the stories of student-athletes, coaches, teams, and the Athletics Department through written, digital, social media, and multimedia platforms. Excellent written, verbal, editing, proofreading, and presentation skills, with the ability to communicate effectively with university administrators, coaches, student-athletes, faculty, staff, media representatives, alumni, donors, and the general public. Ability to manage multiple projects, competing priorities, and strict deadlines while maintaining accuracy, organization, and attention to detail. Ability to develop and maintain consistent messaging, branding, and communications standards across departmental platforms and initiatives. Ability to collaborate effectively with athletics administration, coaches, marketing, creative services, development, ticketing, compliance, and university communications to achieve departmental goals. Ability to work evenings, weekends, holidays, and extended hours as required, including attendance at athletic events, media activities, and postseason competitions. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5575?c=usm": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper I",
      "description": "Groundskeeper I | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Groundskeeper I Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5575 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Groundskeeper I The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Groundskeeper I. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Administration Physical Plant Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 12.71 - 12.71 Pay Grade N02 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Performs ground maintenance tasks to ensure the upkeep of university grounds and related areas. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Plants trees, shrubs,\n     flowers, and grass; trims and edges around walks, flower beds, and walls\n     using clippers and edging tools; prunes shrubs and hedges to shape and\n     improve growth; and rakes and removes leaves. Cleans drainage ditches\n     and culverts; hauls debris to dumping area. Cut lawns using hand mowers, power mowers, or power\n     trimmers/edgers. Clean and maintain sidewalks, parking lots, and\n     other campus grounds. Performs other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree (GED); Three months related experience and/or training relating to grounds or landscape work. Valid Driver's License Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of grounds maintenance practices, plant care, and landscaping principles. Knowledge of the proper use and maintenance of groundskeeping equipment. Skill in using groundskeeping equipment, such as lawnmowers, trimmers, blowers, and edgers. Ability to follow oral and written instructions. Ability to perform manual labor for extended periods in various weather conditions. Ability to communicate and interact effectively with a diverse group of people. Preferred Qualifications One year of grounds or landscape related experience. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
