    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5574?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor- Mathematics",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor- Mathematics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Teaching Professor- Mathematics Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5574 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/24/2026 Back to Search Assistant Teaching Professor- Mathematics The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor- Mathematics. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 54,000.00 - 54,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date December 20, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants\nshould include a cover letter showing evidence of successful professional\nexperience in and knowledge Mathematics, curriculum vitae, a teaching\nstatement, and a list of three professional references (no letters required).  The anticipated start date is August 2, 2027. To ensure full consideration, complete application materials should be\nsubmitted. All questions should be directed to Dr. Bernd Schroeder (Bernd.Schroeder@usm.edu), Search Committee\nChair. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a\nfull-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not\nsponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This\nnine-month, teaching-track faculty position requires teaching undergraduate\nand potentially graduate courses in the School, mentoring students,\nproviding service to the school, college, university, and professional\norganizations, and assisting the program coordinator for the Mathematics\nprogram. Primary Duties and Responsibilities This\nnine-month, teaching-track faculty position requires teaching undergraduate\nand potentially graduate courses in the School, mentoring students,\nproviding service to the school, college, university, and professional\norganizations, and assisting the program coordinator for the Mathematics\nprogram. Teaching\n     undergraduate and graduate coursework in Mathematics. Assisting\n     with program development and needs in coordination with the Mathematics\n     Program Coordinator. Mentoring\n     students toward professional career goals. Participating\n     in service to the university, college, school, community, and professional\n     organizations. Performs\n     other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Mathematics or closely related discipline form an accredited university. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated\n     teaching effectiveness or strong potential for teaching excellence. Strong\n     written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated\n     ability to work effectively and collegially with students, staff, and\n     faculty from all backgrounds, programs, and colleges. Ability\n     to teach undergraduate Mathematics coursework. Commitment\n     to student mentoring and student-centered teaching. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctoral degree or in Mathematics or related field. Experience with student recruitment and program development. Teaching, mentoring, and service experience at the university level. Experience with online course delivery and instruction (Canvas Learning Management System). Active involvement in professional organizations related Mathematics. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5571?c=usm": {
      "title": "Director of Educational Field Experiences and Assistant Teaching Professor",
      "description": "Director of Educational Field Experiences and Assistant Teaching Professor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Director of Educational Field Experiences and Assistant Teaching Professor Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5571 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Director of Educational Field Experiences and Assistant Teaching Professor The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Director of Educational Field Experiences and Assistant Teaching Professor. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Field Experiences Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Director of Educational Field Experiences\nand Assistant Teaching Professor provides leadership and oversight of\neducational field experiences, including student teaching and other clinical\nexperiences, and supports high-quality clinical preparation across Southern\nMiss educator preparation programs. The Director collaborates with academic\nprograms, P–12 partners, clinical educators, and educator preparation\ncolleagues to support effective clinical preparation. The Director leads office\noperations, supervises office staff, and coordinates processes serving teacher\ncandidates and educational partners. The position also contributes to\ndata-informed planning, institutional reporting, and continuous improvement\nassociated with CAEP Standard 2. This full-time, twelve-month, non-tenure-track\nfaculty position requires teaching one course per semester and service to the\nSchool of Education. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Directs the day-to-day operations for educational\n     field experiences, establishes priorities, coordinates office processes,\n     supervises office staff, and supports effective service to teacher\n     candidates, academic programs, and educational partners. Teaches one course per semester for the School of\n     Education and contributes service that supports School of Education\n     programs and priorities. The selected candidate may negotiate a reduced\n     teaching load in the first semester. Provides undergraduate methods classes with\n     information and guidance about the student-teaching semester, registration\n     process, and professional expectations. Provides oversight for licensure candidates\n     completing clinical, practicum, and student-teaching placements. Leads\n     established response processes when concerns arise in partner-school\n     settings, including decisions regarding candidate removal, in collaboration\n     with the candidate, University Supervisor or faculty member, mentor\n     teacher, and school administrators. Maintains accurate information related to\n     clinical, practicum, and student-teaching placements and prepares reports\n     and communications that support planning, decision-making, and\n     institutional requirements. Coordinates, as part of the educator\n     preparation team, work related to CAEP Standard 2, including documentation\n     and continuous improvement involving clinical educators and clinical\n     experiences. Plans and coordinates professional development\n     seminars for teacher candidates each semester. Selects, supervises, and evaluates University\n     Supervisors for the School of Education. Coordinates professional\n     development and ongoing communication for University Supervisors, using\n     current data and guidance from the Mississippi Department of Education,\n     USM’s Professional Education Council, and the School of Education to\n     strengthen student teaching. Oversees training and support for mentor\n     teachers. Selects and engages members of the Educational\n     Field Experiences Advisory Board, which meets twice each school year.\n     Shares information about USM and Mississippi Department of Education\n     requirements and solicits feedback to strengthen partnerships and support\n     continuous improvement in teacher preparation programs. Attends School of Education faculty meetings,\n     participates in the School of Education Curriculum Committee and other\n     school committees, and keeps faculty informed about Educational Field\n     Experiences policies, processes, and initiatives. Directs annual selection processes for\n     student-teaching-abroad opportunities, student-teaching-related\n     scholarships, and awards recognizing teacher candidates, mentor teachers,\n     and administrators. Conducts interviews, coordinates selection, and\n     communicates results to appropriate school and college leadership. Performs other duties relevant to the job as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications A master’s degree or higher in\nelementary education, special education, secondary education, educational\nleadership, curriculum and instruction, or another relevant field. Five years of successful P–12\nclassroom teaching or other directly relevant educational experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated organizational and\nforward-planning skills, including experience managing overlapping work cycles,\nrecurring milestones, deadlines, accurate records, and reliable processes. Excellent written, verbal, and\ninterpersonal communication skills, including experience explaining complex\nprocesses and working with tact and diplomacy across internal and external\nstakeholder groups. Demonstrated ability to foster\na collaborative, service-oriented workplace culture grounded in\nprofessionalism, communication, and shared accountability. Experience monitoring and\ninterpreting data and using digital information systems to support planning,\nreporting, decision-making, and continuous improvement. Knowledge of accreditation or\ninstitutional effectiveness processes or demonstrated ability to learn\napplicable standards; familiarity with CAEP is preferred. Preferred Qualifications Education Specialist (Ed.S.)\ndegree or higher in elementary education. At least 10 years of P–12\nprofessional experience, including classroom teaching and either\nteacher-leadership or school-administration experience. Prior experience teaching or\nsupervising undergraduate teacher education students. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5569?c=usm": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Patrol Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Patrol Officer Long Beach, MS, United States | req5569 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Patrol Officer The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Patrol Officer. Position Details Location Gulf Park 730 East Beach Boulevard Long Beach, Mississippi, 39560 United States Division University Police Gulf Park Div Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N09 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Performs law\nenforcement and police department duties involving the protection of life and\nproperty through the enforcement of state laws and university rules and\nregulations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Responsible for\n     performing law enforcement activities; to include but not limited to enforcing\n     federal, state, and local laws and USM rules and regulations. Responds to all emergency\n     calls involving crimes, disturbances, accidents, personal injuries, fires,\n     and natural disasters. Responsible for\n     investigating crimes and violations of USM rules and regulations,\n     accidents, etc. Engages with the\n     community in proactive police activities to prevent crimes, disorder,\n     property loss, accidents, etc. Responsible for providing\n     a wide range of community services involving traffic and crowd control,\n     security at special events, crisis intervention, referrals, escorts,\n     motorist assistance, public information, emergency notification, and\n     medical assistance. Performs other duties as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications High\nSchool graduate or equivalent G.E.D. Valid\nMississippi Driver’s License Mississippi\nLaw Enforcement Certification or graduate of a Mississippi Law Enforcement\nTraining Academy. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to\nuse a personal computer and associated software, police radio, firearms,\ninvestigative equipment and resources, photographic and video equipment, basic\noffice equipment. Ability to\nuse spreadsheet software and use of video and other software applications. Basic\nknowledge and skill within Windows-based computer and software applications, to\ninclude Microsoft Office applications, and the ability to use email to send and\nreceive correspondence, proficiency in use of search engines. Strong\ncommunication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s\ndegree and/or bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Six months\nto one year of patrol officer experience with a law enforcement agency. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5566?c=usm": {
      "title": "Training Manager",
      "description": "Training Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Training Manager Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5566 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Training Manager The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Training Manager. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Spectator Sports Safety and Security Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Partial Pay Grade E10 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Responsible for the day-to-day supervision of instructional and support\nstaff to include evaluations, scheduling, and administrative oversight for the DHS/FEMA\nsports safety and security training program. Ensures compliance with all\ngrant-related guidelines. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Oversee the course\n     instructor’s selection, training, day-to-day assignment, and\n     performance.  Establish goals and\n     monitor performance for all assigned staff.  Review instructor evaluations on a\n     quarterly basis and provide coaching and/or additional training as needed. Observe and evaluate all\n     instructional staff.  Maintain\n     up-to-date instructor training records. Meet all required performance\n     targets: number of course deliveries and participants, and instructor\n     utilization. This includes marketing efforts to ensure the optimal target\n     market is captured. Manage course\n     coordination efforts and course support to ensure the quality of each\n     delivery within the program. This includes preparing training materials,\n     shipping material, coordinating delivery locations, and ensuring all\n     course forms are completed in a timely manner. Keeps informed of and\n     interprets pertinent rules, regulations, policies, and procedures set\n     forth by the University or other governing agencies and adjust plans as\n     required. Performs\n     other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from\nan accredited college or university in criminal justice, sports management, or a related field and at least 5 years of project management experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability\nto speak effectively before groups of customers or employees of organizations. Skill\nin completing assignments accurately and with attention to detail. Ability\nto communicate and interact effectively with a diverse group of people. Ability\nto analyze, organize and prioritize work while meeting multiple deadlines. Excellent\norganization and time management skills. Ability\nto establish goals and objectives. Preferred Qualifications Master's Degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in criminal justice, sports management, or a related field and at least 8 years of project\nmanagement experience in sports administration, emergency management, law\nenforcement, or a related field. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5565?c=usm": {
      "title": "Supervisor - Records",
      "description": "Supervisor - Records | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Supervisor - Records Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5565 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/23/2026 Back to Search Supervisor - Records The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Supervisor - Records. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Office of the University Registrar Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N06 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The position of Records Supervisor within the Office of\nthe University Registrar involves overseeing the daily operations of the\nRecords area. This role carries the responsibility of managing academic records\nwhile adhering to established security protocols and procedures. The Records\nSupervisor will collaborate with the campus community and external vendors to\nstreamline and optimize student record-related processes, including but not\nlimited to transcript processing, grade and record changes, academic standing\nadjustments, biographical information updates, and the management of imaged\nrecords. In\nthis role, the Records Supervisor plays a crucial part in maintaining the\nintegrity and accuracy of academic records, ensuring compliance with academic\npolicies, and enhancing the overall efficiency of record-related processes. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Supervise Employee Leave Time: Maintain an accurate schedule of personal and sick leave for staff in the records area. Supervision:\n     Oversee the student records section of the Registrar's Office, which\n     includes implementing approved academic policies, ensuring the security of\n     student records, and updating procedures in line with academic policy\n     changes. Business\n     Process Development: Develop and continually update efficient business\n     processes within the student information system for the student records\n     area that include grade/academic record changes, academic standing,\n     updating bio-graphical student information. Document\n     Imaging: Supervise the imaging of documents associated with a student's\n     educational record. Transcript\n     Processing: Supervise the transcript processing section of the Registrar's\n     Office. This involves collaborating with third party vendor to ensure the\n     timely processing of transcript requests, supervising data entry and\n     verifying the accuracy of historical records converted to the current\n     student information system. Also, ensure proper audit procedures are\n     followed for accounting of student transcripts. Perform any other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Associates degree from an Accredited college or University and accumulated three years of hands-on experience in roles requiring strong office management skills and attention to detail. Strong knowledge base of University policies and procedures as it pertains to student enrollment. Working knowledge of campus departments across the University. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Working knowledge of PeopleSoft. Excellent communication, interpersonal and organizational skills. Ability to work with multiple departments across campus. Strong analytical and problem solving skills. Proficient with Microsoft Excel and ability to use Microsoft Word. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree. Three to five years experience working with PeopleSoft. Experience working at a Higher Education Institution. Supervisory experience. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
