    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5534?c=usm": {
      "title": "Instructor, School of Marketing",
      "description": "Instructor, School of Marketing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor, School of Marketing Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5534 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/15/2026 Back to Search Instructor, School of Marketing The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Instructor, School of Marketing. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Marketing Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants To ensure full consideration, completed application materials (including a cover letter, teaching philosophy, and contact information for three professional references) should be submitted to The University of Southern Mississippi website at https://jobs.usm.edu by the priority deadline of Thursday, October 15, 2026. Questions should be directed to Dr. Wei Wang at W.Wang@usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Marketing in the College of Business & Economic Development at The University of Southern Mississippi invites applicants to apply for a nine-month position of Instructor of Marketing beginning in August 2027. This position is for the Hattiesburg campus and will support our growing face-to-face and online Marketing degrees, minors, and certificates. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate courses and, depending on academic credentials and program needs, may have opportunities to teach graduate courses. The position carries a teaching load of 12 semester credit hours per term and includes participation in School events and activities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach four courses per semester (or equivalent) to be determined by the Director of the School. Teaching assignments will primarily support the Marketing BSBA degree, minors, certificates, and related programs. Teach a variety of marketing\n     courses based on program needs, with particular emphasis on Social Media\n     Marketing, Digital Marketing, Integrated Marketing Communications, and/or\n     other courses as needed. Demonstrate a\n     commitment to high-quality teaching in both face-to-face and online\n     learning environments, and contribute service supporting the mission of the School,\n     College, and University. Collaborate effectively with faculty and staff and participate in School events, activities, and initiatives. Additional responsibilities may\n     include managing the School's social media presence and/or the Social\n     Media Minor, mentoring undergraduate students, supporting student\n     recruitment and retention efforts, and performing other duties as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications A minimum of a master's degree in marketing, business, or a closely related field is required by the start of the appointment. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States on a full time and continuing basis without current or future sponsorship. Temporary employment authorizations, including OPT and CPT, do not satisfy this requirement. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to articulate concepts and instructions effectively to students. Capacity to build positive and professional relationships with students and colleagues. Skilled in managing course materials, time, and administrative tasks like grading and answering emails. Familiarity with standard software for communication and online learning platforms. Preferred Qualifications Candidates who demonstrate the following are preferred: Relevant professional experience in marketing. A doctorate in Marketing or a closely related field. Experience developing and delivering face-to-face and online instruction at the undergraduate level, with graduate teaching experience considered when appropriate to the candidate's academic credentials. Experience engaging and supporting diverse student populations and developing relationships with community and business partners. Experience with student recruitment and retention initiatives. Evidence of effective collaboration in academic or professional environments. Relevant teaching experience and demonstrated effectiveness in applied, project-based, or client-based learning. Demonstrated ability to engage students and challenge them to develop the knowledge, skills, and problem-solving abilities needed to become successful marketing professionals. The Mission of the Marketing Program Our faculty maintains active research records and\nconnections with business leaders. We prepare our students to be successful\nmarketing professionals by (a) challenging them to develop the knowledge and\nskills necessary to be effective problem-solvers, and (b) requiring them to\napply their knowledge and skills on client-based projects to gain real-world\nexperience. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
