    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5551?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5551 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Kinesiology and Nutrition Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date August 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026. All questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Paul Donahue (paul.donahue@usm.edu), Search Committee Chair. Applicants should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and 2 statements: (1) research accomplishments and 3-year plan (3 page maximum, not including references), and (2) teaching philosophy (2 page maximum).  Candidates should also provide a list of three professional references and official transcripts indicating all degrees. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Join a growing and dynamic program at The University of Southern Mississippi. The School of Kinesiology and Nutrition invites applications for a tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor position beginning Fall 2027. Based in Hattiesburg, Mississippi, this in-person position seeks an innovative and collaborative scholar with expertise in sport coaching, applications of motor development and/or motor learning, and/or coach development. The successful candidate will develop a productive research agenda, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, mentor students, and contribute to service. Candidates whose interests align with coach preparation, applied motor learning and development, or coach education are especially encouraged to apply. The School of Kinesiology and Nutrition serves more than 600 students and includes 27 faculty and staff. With five undergraduate programs, three master's programs, an active doctoral program, and state-of-the-art research and teaching facilities, the School offers a collaborative environment that supports excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. As a Carnegie R1 institution, USM is committed to excellence across research, teaching, and service. Faculty are supported in building the type of academic career they envision, with opportunities to pursue impactful scholarship while maintaining a healthy and sustainable work-life balance. Combined with the School's close-knit culture, USM and Hattiesburg provide an inviting place for faculty and their families to live, work, and thrive. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop and maintain an active research agenda in sport coaching, applied motor development/motor learning, coach development, or related areas. Pursue scholarly dissemination through high-quality publications, presentations, and external funding opportunities. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the School in face-to-face and online formats. Collaborate with School faculty to enhance curriculum and continuous improvement processes required for accreditation. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students through teaching and research. Participate in school, university, professional, and community service activities. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in Sport Coaching, Kinesiology, Sport Pedagogy, Motor Behavior, Exercise Science, Sport Science, or a closely related field (by August 2027). Evidence of potential to conduct and disseminate high-quality research. Demonstrated potential to teach at the college level. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work effectively as a member of a multidisciplinary team of scientists. Preferred Qualifications Research/expertise in skill acquisition, applied motor behavior, athlete development, and/or sport pedagogy. Experience in coaching sport teams at the high school and/or collegiate level. Experience in teaching graduate courses at the senior college/university level across multiple instructional formats including online and face-to-face. Established or emerging focused program of research with evidence of scholarly productivity. An established research focus demonstrated through both publications and pursuit of extramural funding. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5550?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5550 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor, School of Kinesiology & Nutrition. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Kinesiology and Nutrition Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date August 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026. All questions concerning the position should be directed to Dr. Nuno Oliveira ( nuno.oliveira@usm.edu ), and/or Dr. Alicia Landry ( alicia.landry@usm.edu ), Search Committee Co-Chairs. Applicants should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and 2 statements: (1) research accomplishments and 3-year plan (3 page maximum, not including references), and (2) teaching philosophy (2 page maximum).  Candidates should also provide a list of three professional references and official transcripts indicating all degrees. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Join a growing and dynamic program at The University of Southern Mississippi. The School of Kinesiology and Nutrition invites applications for two tenure-track, nine-month Assistant Professor positions beginning Fall 2027. Located in Hattiesburg, Mississippi, these in-person positions offer an exciting opportunity for innovative, collaborative scholars with expertise in cardiovascular physiology, exercise science, nutrition, or related fields that complement and enhance our School's academic and research programs. The successful candidate will develop a productive research agenda, teach undergraduate and graduate courses, mentor students, and contribute to service. We particularly welcome applications from candidates whose scholarly interests and expertise are aligned with cardiovascular physiology, applied exercise physiology, exercise science, nutrition, or other complementary areas that support interdisciplinary collaboration and innovation. The School of Kinesiology and Nutrition serves more than 600 students and includes 27 faculty and staff. With five undergraduate programs, three master's programs, an active doctoral program, and state-of-the-art research and teaching facilities, the School offers a collaborative environment that supports excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. As a Carnegie R1 institution, USM is committed to excellence across research, teaching, and service. Faculty are supported in building the type of academic career they envision, with opportunities to pursue impactful scholarship while maintaining a healthy and sustainable work-life balance. Combined with the School's close-knit culture, USM and Hattiesburg provide an inviting place for faculty and their families to live, work, and thrive. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop and maintain an active research agenda in cardiovascular physiology, exercise physiology, exercise science, nutrition/dietetics, or a related field. Pursue scholarly dissemination through high-quality publications, presentations, and external funding opportunities. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in the School in face-to-face and online formats. Collaborate with School faculty to enhance curriculum and continuous improvement processes required for accreditation. Mentor undergraduate and graduate students through teaching and research. Participate in school, university, professional, and community service activities. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in Exercise Physiology, Exercise Science, Kinesiology, Nutrition/Dietetics, or a closely related field (by August 2027). Evidence of potential to conduct and disseminate high-quality research. Demonstrated potential to teach at the college level. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work effectively as a member of a multidisciplinary team of scientists. Preferred Qualifications Research/expertise in translational research. Licensure and/or professional certifications relevant to the candidate's discipline (e.g., ACSM, RDN, CSCS, or equivalent). Experience in teaching graduate courses at the senior college/university level across multiple instructional formats including online and face-to-face. Established or emerging focused program of research with evidence of scholarly productivity. An established research focus demonstrated through both publications and pursuit of extramural funding. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5540?c=usm": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor - School of Construction and Design",
      "description": "Academic Advisor - School of Construction and Design | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Advisor - School of Construction and Design Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5540 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Academic Advisor - School of Construction and Design The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Academic Advisor - School of Construction and Design. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Construction and Design Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 41,000.00 - 41,000.00 Pay Grade X06 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please submit your  and three references to apply for this position. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Academic Advisor works to cultivate student success by 1) assisting students in their transition to the University, 2) facilitating students’ efforts to plan their path to degree, 3) promoting engagement in their major and 4) connecting students with key campus resources.  In addition to working with students in their caseload, advisors will also respond to walk-in student needs, provide support to faculty advisors, and assist with undergraduate recruitment and retention initiatives. The position of advisor is a full-time (40 hour/week) position and limited evenings and/or weekend hours are expected. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Work collaboratively and effectively with other advisors, staff, and faculty in the School, utilizing evidence-based best practices for advising to increase student success. Meet with students to advise them in matters pertaining to academic requirements and progression toward degree completion; proactively reach out to students to ensure they are meeting expectations; refer students to resources on campus as appropriate and ensure student issues are addressed efficiently and effectively; respond to student questions, including walk-ins, emails, phone, and videoconferencing, with a helpful attitude, correct information, and timeliness; Provide backup for faculty advisors in the unit when faculty are not available or at the request of the school director. Assist students and faculty advisors with University processes such as course substitutions, undergraduate exception requests, and graduation applications.  Work with students as necessary to complete Academic Improvement Plans and Academic Clearance forms. Coordinate and participate in undergraduate recruitment, orientation, and retention events and initiatives. Engage in professional development and training to improve advising skills, including recognizing and supporting the needs of diverse student populations, and perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university and at least one year experience working in an academic environment or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent communication skills (oral and written) Commitment to professional development and growth Ability to work independently to manage caseloads, demonstrating strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and time management Knowledge of academic policies/procedures and major/degree plans according to the advisor’s area, in addition to student resources throughout the University Flexibility in using problem-solving skills and initiative to assist individual students with particular issues and identify methods to improve office processes and systems Ability to work effectively as a team member and develop collaborative and productive professional relationships in pursuit of shared goals Skill in working with diverse students to foster an inclusive community that recognizes the value of all people, regardless of ethnicity, race, gender, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, ability, or socioeconomic status Preferred Qualifications Prior experience with advisement, student coaching, or other student academic support work, especially with diverse student populations. Master’s degree from an accredited college or university. Educational background in a field related to higher education, student services, or counseling. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5530?c=usm": {
      "title": "Grant Specialist I - CRPE (part-time)",
      "description": "Grant Specialist I - CRPE (part-time) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Grant Specialist I - CRPE (part-time) United States | req5530 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Grant Specialist I - CRPE (part-time) The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Grant Specialist I - CRPE (part-time). Position Details Location Generic Location United States Division School of Education Position Type Staff Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 37.50 - 37.50 Pay Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a 1-page description of your experience implementing school-wide PBIS systems. This position will support schools in implementing and sustaining Tier 1 of a Multi-Tiered System\nof Supports (MTSS) and Positive Behavioral Interventions and Supports (PBIS)\nframework with fidelity. Responsibilities include coaching, training,\ndata analysis, systems development, and continuous improvement support. We anticipate hiring one part-time specialist by October 2026 and two additional part-time specialists by July 2027. Extensive travel required, sometimes overnight. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The PART-TIME Grant Specialist I will work in grant-funded projects within the Center for Research to Practice in Education (CRPE) at Southern Miss.  Currently, this role includes extensive work with the Mississippi State Personnel Development Grant (REACH MS) to support Educator Preparation Programs around the state in the development of Registered Teacher Apprenticeship Programs in Special Education.  The Grant Specialist I will provide training, coaching, and technical assistance to educator preparation programs, districts, mentors, and workforce partners. The specialist will help align coursework, field experiences, mentorship, candidate assessment, and program approval processes with evidence-based practices and state requirements while supporting implementation fidelity, continuous improvement, sustainability, and statewide scaling. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Deliver evidence-based professional learning, technical assistance, and coaching to educators and other participants involved in state and federally funded grant initiatives. Support implementation of grant-funded activities by assisting schools, districts, and partner organizations in implementing evidence-based practices with fidelity. Provide coaching and consultation using established implementation frameworks, coaching models, and project procedures. Assist participants in collecting, analyzing, and utilizing implementation, fidelity, and outcome data to support continuous improvement and informed decision-making. Develop and maintain collaborative working relationships with educators, administrators, families, community partners, and other project stakeholders. Assist with planning, coordination, and implementation of meetings, trainings, conferences, and other project activities. Collect, organize, and maintain project documentation, implementation records, participation data, and other information required for grant reporting and evaluation. Assist in preparing reports, presentations, dissemination materials, and other project deliverables in accordance with grant requirements. Ensure assigned responsibilities are completed in compliance with university, state, federal, and sponsor policies, procedures, and grant requirements. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's\ndegree from an accredited college or university in education, special\neducation, behavioral sciences, psychology, counseling, social work, or a\nrelated field; or an equivalent combination of education and directly related\nprofessional experience. Two (2)\nyears of experience providing educational, behavioral, instructional, or\nrelated services in PK–12 educational settings. Current,\nvalid Mississippi teaching license or eligibility to obtain such licensure\nwithin six (6) months of employment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of evidence-based\n     instructional, behavioral, and implementation practices. Ability to develop and deliver\n     effective professional learning, coaching, and technical assistance. Strong written, verbal, and\n     interpersonal communication skills. Ability to establish and\n     maintain collaborative working relationships with educators,\n     administrators, community partners, and project stakeholders. Strong organizational, project\n     coordination, and time management skills. Ability to analyze\n     implementation and outcome data to support continuous improvement. Ability to work independently\n     while managing multiple priorities, deadlines, and travel schedules. Proficiency with Microsoft\n     Office applications, Google Workspace, learning management systems,\n     virtual meeting platforms, and other technology used to support grant\n     implementation. Preferred Qualifications Master's\ndegree in special education, education, behavioral sciences, psychology,\ncounseling, social work, or a related field. Three (3) or\nmore years of experience providing educational, behavioral, instructional, or\nrelated services in PK–12 educational settings. Two (2) or\nmore years of experience delivering professional learning, technical\nassistance, or coaching for educators. Experience\nimplementing evidence-based instructional, behavioral, or school improvement\ninitiatives. Experience\nworking on state or federally funded grants. Experience\ncollecting, analyzing, and utilizing implementation or outcome data to support\ncontinuous improvement. Experience\nusing learning management systems, virtual meeting platforms, and other\ninstructional technology to support professional learning. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5521?c=usm": {
      "title": "Data Scientist II",
      "description": "Data Scientist II | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Data Scientist II Gulfport, MS, United States | req5521 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/14/2026 Back to Search Data Scientist II The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Data Scientist II. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Pay Grade E12 Posting Close Date November 30, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Must be able to obtain a TWIC (Transportation Workers Identification Credential) Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Data Scientist II\ndevelops and implements statistical, mathematical, computer programming,\noperations research, and diagnostic methods and techniques to interpret and\nanalyze complex data. This position exercises independent judgment under\nlimited supervision from a higher-level scientist or technical supervisor, with\nwork activities planned, reviewed, and evaluated through regular consultation\nwith leadership. The role supports research, development, testing, and\nevaluation activities related to ocean sensing buoys and uncrewed surface and\nsubsurface marine vehicles, including platform systems, payloads, command and\ncontrol systems, power systems, and data integration and analysis. This\nposition is located at the Roger F. Wicker Center for Ocean Enterprise in\nGulfport, Mississippi and collaborates with industry, academic, state, and\nfederal partners in support of ocean technology and research initiatives. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Conduct research to advance hardware, software, and techniques to develop computational algorithms and statistical methods that find patterns and relationships in large volumes of data. Manage, collect, visualize, analyze, and summarize data, data reports, experiments, and field activities. Support preparation for peer-reviewed publications, including maps, tables, and other illustrative materials. Perform server maintenance, database administration, data pipelines creation, and web front end development. Contribute to Ocean Enterprise goals by participating in developing proposals, keeping appropriate individuals on the OE staff informed of activities and providing status reports documenting milestones regarding ongoing projects. Participate in test and evaluation of UxS, other autonomous or semi-autonomous vehicles or platforms and perform analysis of data collected. Provides programmatic and technical support to project directors or principal investigators and collaborates with Ocean Enterprise, USM and external researchers as appropriate. Performs other duties as\nassigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in data science, engineering, computer science, remote sensing,\nphysical science or related field. andsix (6) years of experience in data\nscience research, applications, or a similar occupation. Two (2) years of related\neducation and related experience may be substituted on an equal basis. Must be\na US Citizen or US Person and have a valid Driver’s License. Must be able to\nobtain Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to read, analyze, and\n     interpret research periodicals, professional journals, and technical\n     procedures associated with research activities. Strong written communication\n     skills necessary to perform assigned duties and prepare technical\n     documentation and reports Ability to effectively present\n     information and respond to questions from data science professionals,\n     stakeholders, and the public Ability to process, visualize,\n     analyze, and interpret various geospatial datasets and perform field work\n     aboard small and large vessels Proficiency with programming languages, platforms, and\nsoftware libraries including Python,Java, ROS, R and RStudio, MATLAB, Amazon\nWeb Services SageMaker, Microsoft Azure, Google Cloud Platform, TensorFlow,\nKeras, Scikit Learn, Pandas, BASH, Apache, Parquet, Protocol Buffers, Nginx,\nNumPy, SQL, NoSQL databases including MongoDB, ArcPy, Tableau, Docker, and\nArcGIS Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in data science, engineering, remote sensing, physical science, or\nrelated field. And two (2) years of experience in data science or related\nresearch. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5545?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Computer Science | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor in Computer Science Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5545 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/11/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor in Computer Science The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor in Computer Science. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Computing Sciences and Computer Engineering Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Transcripts should be uploaded with the application. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Computing Sciences and Computer Engineering (CSCE) in the College of Arts and Sciences at The University of Southern Mississippi is seeking applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position. The position will be based at the University's main campus in Hattiesburg. The School of CSCE offers undergraduate programs in Computer Science, Cyber Security, Information Technology, and Computer Engineering and M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Computer Science. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate classes in computer science, supporting program growth in artificial intelligence and intelligent systems. Develop an externally-funded research program. Provide service to the School, College, and University. Provide mentorship to graduate students. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in Computer Science or a closely related field and must demonstrate the potential to establish a high quality research program, collaborate effectively with others, and excel in teaching. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong oral and written communication skills and evidence of ability to publish high-quality peer-reviewed research and secure external funding. Preferred Qualifications One to three years teaching experience in higher education. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5538?c=usm": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist, School of Social Work",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist, School of Social Work | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Administrative Specialist, School of Social Work Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5538 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/11/2026 Back to Search Administrative Specialist, School of Social Work The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Administrative Specialist, School of Social Work. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Social Work Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N04 Posting Close Date January 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants We\nare seeking applicants for an administrative specialist position in the School\nof Social Work. Please submit a resume and the names\nof three references (preferably those who were previous supervisors).\nContact Dr. Michelle Brazeal (michelle.brazeal@usm.edu), Interim Director of\nthe School of Social Work, for more information about the position. Details\nabout the School of Social Work can be found here: www.usm.edu/social-work. Application review will\nbegin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Job Summary This position is for Academic, Operational, and Budgetary Support of the\nSchool Director, faculty, staff, and students. This position is essential, as\nit is the first point of contact for anyone within the School, the public, and\nthe university community. Primary Job Duties and Responsibilities Acts as academic support for the School to include, but not\nlimited to, corresponding with prospective students, coordinating on-campus\nstudent visits, preparing and sending necessary student forms, maintaining\nappropriate student files, and working with faculty, staff, students, and the\nuniversity community to assure student success. Liaises with\noffices/departments/programs that offer courses through ISPD, e.g., all Student\nAffairs courses, Luckyday Scholarship Program, and the Center for Faculty\nDevelopment. Assists\nwith the preparation of and input of course schedules, room reservations, and\nstudent scheduling needs. Manages all class enrollment permissions. Oversees\ntextbook ordering. Organizes summer programs, including conferences. Supports the Internship Office by maintaining and reviewing\ncontracts between the School and external partner agencies, coordinating and\nscheduling required training, maintaining students' required documentation, and\nsubmitting necessary paperwork to outside agencies to facilitate student\nplacements. Serves\nas facility and inventory point of contact. Maintains and tracks school\ninventory. Conducts regular inventory audits. Assists in state-mandated audits.\nOrders course and lab supplies and coordinates delivery, as requested. Process\nnecessary forms for school maintenance, supply purchases, awards, etc. through\nthe University and Foundation. Serve as building liaison, enter work orders,\nand interact with physical plant on building maintenance and services. Manage personnel actions under the supervision of the\nDirector, including creating job requisitions and onboarding and offboarding of\nstaff, faculty, graduate assistants, and temporary non-students. Prepare\nappropriate HR hiring paperwork for faculty, staff, adjuncts, student\nemployees, etc. Prepares credentialing paperwork for instructors. Hires,\nassigns duties, and supervises the work of student employees. Prepares semesterly\npaperwork for Graduate school, including tuition waiver requests, offer\nletters, and Personnel Action Forms. Provides\nadministrative support for the Director, including, but not limited to:\ngathering, analyzing, and/or entering data; event planning and public\nrelations; website management, calendar/scheduling, and facilities\nreservations; correspondence; and preparing reports for accreditation and\nfunding agencies. Serves as back-up and support to fill in as needed by\ncompleting cross-training on all job duties and responsibilities outlined in\nthis position; performs other duties as assigned by the School Director. Minimum Qualifications High\nschool diploma or general education degree (GED) and two years of office\nexperience – OR- an equivalent combination of education and experience. Knowledge,\nSkills, and Abilities (KSA) Proficiency with a PC and keyboard to perform data entry, manipulation, and analysis. Ability to read and interpret documents such as safety rules, operating and maintenance instructions, and procedure manuals. Ability to write routine reports and correspondence in Microsoft Office. Ability to maintain cooperative relationships with colleagues Excellent interpersonal, organizational, oral and written communication skills. Ability to exercise discretion, confidentiality, and judgment in dealing with sensitive issues. Ability to problem solve under direction of school and campus administrators. Preferred\nQualifications Experience working in academia. Minimum\nthree years in a full-time office administration position. Knowledge of SOAR,\nSOARHR, SOARFIN, Cornerstone, BlackBaud, University Foundation Go! System,\nAstra, and Faculty Enlight. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5519?c=usm": {
      "title": "Groundskeeper II",
      "description": "Groundskeeper II | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Groundskeeper II Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5519 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/11/2026 Back to Search Groundskeeper II The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Groundskeeper II. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Administration Physical Plant Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 12.71 - 13.00 Pay Grade N02 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Performs complex ground maintenance tasks to ensure the upkeep of university grounds and related areas. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Plants trees, shrubs,\n     flowers, and grass; trims and edges around walks, flower beds, and walls\n     using clippers and edging tools; prunes shrubs and hedges to shape and\n     improve growth; and rakes and removes leaves. Cleans drainage ditches\n     and culverts; hauls debris to dumping area. Cut lawns using hand mowers, power mowers, power\n     equipment, or tractors equipped with attachments. Picks up trash and debris\n     from campus grounds, streets, and walks. Sprays lawns, shrubs, beds, and trees with herbicides. Assists in athletic grounds duties as assigned Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications High school diploma or general education degree (GED); One-year experience and/or training relating to grounds or landscape work. Valid Driver’s License required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to understand and follow instructions. Skill in completing assignments accurately and with attention to detail. Ability to work overtime when needed. Knowledge of applicable safety requirements. Knowledge of, or the ability to learn, university policies and procedures. Knowledge of the planting and care of trees, shrubbery, flowers, and grass. Skill in the use of grounds-keeping hand tools and equipment, in the operation of motorized and gas-operated equipment. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
