    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5497?c=usm": {
      "title": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Counseling)",
      "description": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Counseling) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Counseling) Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5497 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/9/2026 Back to Search Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Counseling) The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Counseling). Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Psychology Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 1st but we welcome applications anytime and\nwill continue to review as received until the position is filled. Contact Dr. Emily Bullock Yowell to inquire about\nthe position at Emily.Yowell@usm.edu. A completed application will include\n1) a cover letter describing strengths and qualifications for the position, 2)\na CV, 3) names and contact information for three references (letters will be\nrequested following initial review), and 4) academic transcripts (unofficial\ntranscripts are acceptable). Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The University of Southern Mississippi School of Psychology invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. As a scientist-practitioner program within a large, research-active School of Psychology, we seek colleagues who are committed to high-quality teaching, research, service, and clinical training. Faculty benefit from a collaborative and supportive environment, opportunities for community -engaged research with diverse and underserved populations, and strong institutional support for developing and sustaining productive research programs. Resources include college-level assistance in securing external funding and access to a large undergraduate participation pool. Additional resources are available through the University’s Center for Faculty Development, which provides professional development opportunities in teaching, mentoring, scholarship, and leadership for faculty at all career stages. We foster a culture of mentorship, collegiality, and work-life balance, with support for faculty development throughout the tenure and promotion process. We welcome applicants who are eager to advance their research programs while contributing to the School’s collegial, student-centered community. Southern Miss offers faculty the opportunity to contribute to the success of first-generation and diverse college students through teaching, mentorship, research, and clinical training. Faculty contribute across the School’s academic offerings, including teaching courses for our large undergraduate major and clinical training within our graduate programs, often drawing on their own research and clinical expertise. Research mentoring provides additional opportunities to support students’ professional development outside the classroom. Faculty are also encouraged to engage in university service through admissions, professional development, and committee work, contributing to growth and success of or programs. Clinical training includes on-campus supervision of master’s students in external clinical placements and faculty-supervised practica through our in-house training clinic, the Center for Behavioral Health (CBH). The CBH’s state-of-the-art video system supports high-quality supervision, while its diverse clientele provides students with experience working with a broad range of presenting concerns and populations. The CBH also facilitates research collaborations among faculty and students across the School. For applied faculty, Mississippi’s licensure requirements do not include postdoctoral supervised experience, enabling a more streamlined path to professional licensure. The School of Psychology enrolls approximately 600 undergraduate majors and 125 graduate students across three APA -accredited doctoral programs (Counseling, Clinical, and School Psychology), a doctoral program in Experimental Psychology, and a MPCAC-accredited master’s program in Counseling Psychology. Graduate curricula are intentionally coordinated to provide opportunities for students from different disciplines to learn alongside one another and develop an appreciation for interdisciplinary collaboration. We seek colleagues who will contribute to our team-oriented culture and advance the School’s mission. More information can be found at www.usm.edu/psychology. Primary\nDuties and Responsibilities Develop\nand maintain a robust program of research. Teach\nundergraduate and graduate classes, including graduate level practicum courses. Obtain\nlicensure in the state of Mississippi (note that MS does\nnot require postdoctoral hours). Seek\nextramural funding. Contribute\nto the mission of the university and profession through service activities. Perform\nother duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications include a doctoral degree in counseling psychology or related fields (by August 2027) and completion of an APA-accredited predoctoral internship. Applicants must be eligible for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Mississippi. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exceptional written\nand oral communication and interpersonal skills. Proven track\nrecord of innovative teaching practices and the ability to teach\neffectively at the university level in an undergraduate and graduate psychology\nprogram. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and collegially\nwith students, staff, and faculty from all backgrounds, programs, and colleges. Knowledge of the field of Psychology and associated research\nmethodologies, teaching, and scholarly tools. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of, or potential for, conducting research, obtaining extramural funding, and high-quality teaching and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5527?c=usm": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor – Special Education",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor – Special Education | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Visiting Assistant Professor – Special Education Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5527 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Visiting Assistant Professor – Special Education The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Visiting Assistant Professor – Special Education. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Education Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position can be directed to Dr. Danny Guillory (John.Guillory@usm.edu). A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing applicant strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) the names and contact information of three individuals who can provide a recommendation, and 4) academic transcripts (unofficial are accepted but official transcripts are preferred and are necessary for hire). Application materials can be uploaded to the HR site found here: https://jobs.usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Education at The University of Southern Mississippi (USM) invites applicants for one visiting (non tenure track) Assistant Professor position beginning in August 2027 with requirements to be physically present on the Hattiesburg campus. The Education faculty currently provide training to candidates in Elementary, Secondary, and Special Education. We are especially interested in candidates whose experience includes bridging research and practice in K-12 special education settings. We seek a colleague who is committed to preparing high-quality special education professionals, advancing inclusive practices, and contributing to program innovation and growth. Program delivery includes face-to-face, online, and hybrid formats. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaching undergraduate and graduate-level courses in special education. Advising and mentoring students. Providing service to the program, school, university, and profession. Collaborating with faculty colleagues on program development and improvement. Taking on opportunities for leadership in shaping the direction of the special education program. Performing other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in Special Education or closely related field (by August 2027). Two (2) or more years of full-time licensed teaching experience with standards-based curriculum within special education settings. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent written and oral communication skills and the ability to communicate with diverse groups of individuals in a timely manner. Ability to work with a diverse team in multiple settings. Experience with online learning platforms. Experience setting clear performance expectations and provision of meaningful feedback. Preferred Qualifications University teaching experience. Experience in graduate program development, accreditation processes, or innovative program design. Experience with alternative pathways or flexible models of educator preparation. Experience working with schools, agencies, or community partners that support students with disabilities. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5526?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor – Educational Administration and Supervision",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor – Educational Administration and Supervision | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Teaching Professor – Educational Administration and Supervision Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5526 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Teaching Professor – Educational Administration and Supervision The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor – Educational Administration and Supervision. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Education Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position can be directed to Dr. Danny Guillory (john.guillory@usm.edu). A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing applicant strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) the names and contact information of three individuals who can provide a recommendation, and 4) academic transcripts (unofficial are accepted but official transcripts are preferred and are necessary for hire). Application materials can be uploaded to the HR site found here: https://jobs.usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Education at The University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for one teaching (non tenure track) faculty position in educational administration beginning August 2027. This is an on-campus position. The successful candidates will join a collegial faculty community that includes established senior faculty as well as recently appointed colleagues. They will teach and mentor graduate students pursuing either their Educational Specialist (EdS) or Doctorate of Education (EdD) degrees in educational administration offered fully online in synchronous and asynchronous formats. Southern Miss combines the research opportunities of a Carnegie R1 university with the personal connections of a close-knit, interdisciplinary academic community. New faculty join a School of Education that values meaningful scholarship, excellent graduate teaching, cross-program collaboration, and intentional support for faculty development. Hattiesburg offers the cultural and educational amenities of a university city along with short commutes, affordable housing, historic neighborhoods, a strong local arts and restaurant community, and convenient access to the Gulf Coast and New Orleans. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaching and mentoring graduate students in educational administration classes. Contributing to the mission of the university and profession through service activities. Engaging with community partner districts and schools. Performing other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications The ideal candidate for this position will have: A doctoral degree in Educational Administration or closely related field (by August 2027). Five years of educational leadership experience at the school level to include principalship. Evidence of experience in P-12 improvement and methods to assess improvement. Evidence of scholarly potential. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience setting clear performance expectations and provision of meaningful feedback in higher education. Experience and/or familiarity with technology use, particularly in the online learning environment in higher education. Demonstrated ability to deliver accurate, concise and quality communication (verbal and written) in a timely manner to a diverse population. Demonstrated expertise in school improvement, strategic planning, or data-driven decision-making. Strong interpersonal, communication, and collaborative skills with faculty and school partners. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching graduate courses in educational administration. Experience mentoring doctoral students in research, action research, capstone, or dissertation work. Experience mentoring emerging leaders About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5525?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor – Educational Research and Statistics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor – Educational Research and Statistics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor – Educational Research and Statistics Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5525 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor – Educational Research and Statistics The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor – Educational Research and Statistics. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Education Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026 and will continue until the positions are filled. Inquiries about the position can be directed to Dr. Thomas Lipscomb (Thomas.Lipscomb@usm.edu). A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing applicant strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) the names and contact information of three individuals who can provide a recommendation, and 4) academic transcripts (unofficial are accepted but official transcripts are preferred and are necessary for hire). Application materials can be uploaded to the HR site found here: https://jobs.usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Education at The University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for two tenure-track faculty positions in educational research beginning August 2027. These are on-campus positions. The successful candidates will join a collegial faculty community that includes established senior faculty as well as recently appointed colleagues. They will teach and mentor graduate students in an active Ph.D. program in Research, Evaluation, Statistics, and Assessment (RESA), offered on campus and fully online, while providing research-methodology expertise across the School of Education. They will also contribute to the growth and visibility of the recently redesigned M.S. in Educational Data Analytics, which prepares students to use data, research, evaluation, and analytic methods to inform decision-making across educational, organizational, and community settings. Areas of research interest are open. These positions will be especially appealing to scholars who enjoy graduate mentoring, collaboration, and applying rigorous research and analytic methods to consequential questions in education and related fields. Southern Miss combines the research opportunities of a Carnegie R1 university with the personal connections of a close-knit, interdisciplinary academic community. New faculty join a School of Education that values meaningful scholarship, excellent graduate teaching, cross-program collaboration, and intentional support for faculty development. Hattiesburg offers the cultural and educational amenities of a university city along with short commutes, affordable housing, historic neighborhoods, a strong local arts and restaurant community, and convenient access to the Gulf Coast and New Orleans. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaching and mentoring graduate students in research classes across programs. Contributing to the mission of the university and profession through service activities. Conducting and disseminating high-quality independent research. Performing other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. degree in Educational Research, Educational Psychology, or closely related field (by August 2027). Evidence of scholarly potential Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Experience setting clear performance expectations and provision of meaningful feedback in higher education Experience and/or familiarity with technology use, particularly in the online learning environment in higher education Demonstrated ability to deliver accurate, concise and quality communication (verbal and written) in a timely manner to a diverse population Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching graduate educational or interdisciplinary research and/or statistics courses. Preparation to teach measurement; advanced quantitative and data-analytic courses, including data science, machine learning, data-informed inquiry, visualization and reporting, and decision support; survey and mixed-methods research; or other quantitative areas. Experience mentoring student research. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5524?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, School of Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, School of Management | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, School of Management Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5524 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, School of Management The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor, School of Management. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Management Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants The School of Management within the College of Business and Economic Development at The University of Southern Mississippi—a Carnegie R1 Top-Tier Research Institution—invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Management starting in August 2027. To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit all completed application materials online via the official USM job board at https://www.usm.edu/employment-human-resources/applicants-careers.php by the priority deadline of September 10, 2026. Please direct any formal inquiries or questions regarding this position to Dr. Robert Overstreet (Robert.Overstreet@usm.edu), Director of the School of Management. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Management within the College of Business and Economic Development at The University of Southern Mississippi—a Carnegie R1 Top-Tier Research Institution—invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Management starting in August 2027. This role will support our undergraduate and graduate programs. The role includes research, teaching, student mentoring, and active engagement within the professional community. We seek a dynamic faculty member who brings significant professional experience in management to bridge classroom concepts with real-world industry practice. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Conduct quality research and publish in well-respected journals. Teach three courses per semester (or equivalent), including undergraduate and graduate courses in management as determined by the Director of the School. Deliver high-quality teaching across both online and in-person formats, with a focus on designing and delivering impactful experiential learning opportunities. Contribute actively to curriculum development to ensure all course offerings maintain strict relevance and alignment with current industry trends. Partner with faculty across the institution to successfully integrate management concepts into wider interdisciplinary university programs. Maintain an active professional development and networking presence within the regional and national community. Mentor undergraduate students, support undergraduate research initiatives, assist with student recruitment, and participate in service activities across the School, College, and University. Perform other duties as assigned by leadership. Minimum Qualifications A\n conferred PhD in management or other explicitly business-related \ndiscipline from an AACSB-accredited institution by August 2027. A promising record of high-quality research and publication. Documented evidence of serving as the Instructor of Record for at least two university-level courses. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Deep knowledge of management principles, practices, and contemporary industry trends. Knowledge of instructional design and classroom management for both traditional and online delivery formats. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills, including the ability to provide timely and effective student feedback. Skill in utilizing Learning Management Systems (such as Canvas), online teaching tools, and standard office productivity suites (Microsoft Office). Demonstrated ability to build relationships, interact productively, and communicate respectfully with a highly diverse student body and staff population. Preferred Qualifications At least three continuous years of full-time professional experience in a management or leadership role within industry. A passion for recruiting and retaining students. The ability to build diverse student connections and business partnerships. The drive to contribute to a highly collaborative team environment. The\n     ability to guide students into becoming professional problem solvers. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5523?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Elementary Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Elementary Education | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor - Elementary Education Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5523 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor - Elementary Education The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor - Elementary Education. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Education Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position can be directed to Dr. Stacy Reeves (Stacy.Reeves@usm.edu). A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing applicant strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) the names and contact information of three individuals who can provide a recommendation, 4) a teaching philosophy, and 5) academic transcripts (unofficial are accepted but official transcripts are preferred and are necessary for hire). Application materials can be uploaded to the HR site found here: https://jobs.usm.edu. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Education at The University of Southern Mississippi (USM) invites applicants for one (1) full-time, tenure-track, Assistant Professor position, beginning August 2027 with requirements to be present on campus. The research area of specialization for this position is open; preferred areas include math education or literacy education. Our faculty have established records of scholarship in culturally responsive education, multilingual learners, educational equity, multimodal composition, and inquiry, among others. We aim to recruit applicants who will produce impactful research and who will emphasize training to initial licensure candidates in the areas of elementary education to become technologically competent, culturally responsive educators who have an impact on the learning of P-12 students. Additionally, the successful applicant will effectively enrich in-service teachers attending our master’s program in Curriculum and Instruction. Qualified applicants will be prepared to contribute to the School of Education's research, service, and teaching missions at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Southern Miss combines the research opportunities of a Carnegie R1 university with the personal connections of a close-knit, interdisciplinary academic community. New faculty join a School of Education that values meaningful scholarship, excellent teaching, cross-program collaboration, and intentional support for faculty development. The School of Education’s Curriculum and Instruction and Elementary Education programs include bachelor's and master's degrees and include face-to-face, online, and hybrid delivery formats. Hattiesburg and the Gulf Coast campuses offer the cultural and educational amenities of a university city along with short commutes, affordable housing, historic neighborhoods, a strong local arts and restaurant community, and convenient access to New Orleans and other cities. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Developing a strong, independent research program. Collaborating with colleagues on program development and enhancement of pre-service and in-service teacher education programs. Teaching and mentoring students across programs. Seeking external funding. Contributing to the mission of the university and profession through service activities. Performing other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in Curriculum and Instruction, Elementary Education, or a closely related field (must be completed by August 2027). If the degree is in a related field, a clear focus on elementary education is required. Two (2) or more years of full-time licensed teaching experience with standards-based curriculum in an elementary general education classroom. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated ability to deliver accurate, concise and quality communication (verbal and written) in a timely manner to a diverse population. Experience setting clear performance expectations and provision of meaningful feedback. Experience and/or familiarity with technology use, particularly in the online learning environment. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated excellence or potential for excellence in scholarship and research. Experience teaching mathematics, reading, or other inclusive practices in elementary settings. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5522?c=usm": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer",
      "description": "Patrol Officer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Patrol Officer Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5522 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Patrol Officer The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Patrol Officer. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division University Police Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N09 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Performs law\nenforcement and police department duties involving the protection of life and\nproperty through the enforcement of state laws and university rules and\nregulations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Responsible for\n     performing law enforcement activities; to include but not limited to enforcing\n     federal, state, and local laws and USM rules and regulations. Responds to all emergency\n     calls involving crimes, disturbances, accidents, personal injuries, fires,\n     and natural disasters. Responsible for\n     investigating crimes and violations of USM rules and regulations,\n     accidents, etc. Engages with the\n     community in proactive police activities to prevent crimes, disorder,\n     property loss, accidents, etc. Responsible for providing\n     a wide range of community services involving traffic and crowd control,\n     security at special events, crisis intervention, referrals, escorts,\n     motorist assistance, public information, emergency notification, and\n     medical assistance. Performs other duties as\n     assigned. Minimum Qualifications High\nSchool graduate or equivalent G.E.D. Valid\nMississippi Driver’s License Mississippi\nLaw Enforcement Certification or graduate of a Mississippi Law Enforcement\nTraining Academy. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to\nuse a personal computer and associated software, police radio, firearms,\ninvestigative equipment and resources, photographic and video equipment, basic\noffice equipment. Ability to\nuse spreadsheet software and use of video and other software applications. Basic\nknowledge and skill within Windows-based computer and software applications, to\ninclude Microsoft Office applications, and the ability to use email to send and\nreceive correspondence, proficiency in use of search engines. Strong\ncommunication and interpersonal skills. Preferred Qualifications Associate’s\ndegree and/or bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university. Six months\nto one year of patrol officer experience with a law enforcement agency. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5516?c=usm": {
      "title": "Electrical Engineer II",
      "description": "Electrical Engineer II | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Electrical Engineer II Gulfport, MS, United States | req5516 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Electrical Engineer II The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Electrical Engineer II. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division VP Research Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 64,124.00 - 86,755.00 Pay Grade E13 Posting Close Date October 26, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This mid-level position is responsible for the design, integration, testing, troubleshooting, and field support of electrical and electronic systems for Remotely Operated Vehicles (ROVs), Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs), and related subsea equipment. The role requires hands-on technical work from concept through component level, strong troubleshooting skills, and the ability to support both shop and offshore operations. Work is performed under general supervision as part of a multidisciplinary subsea robotics team supporting research and operational missions. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Design and develop electrical systems and circuits for subsea robotics equipment, including power distribution, control systems, sensors, and communications, from concept through component level. Create and maintain accurate electrical schematics, wiring diagrams, bills of materials, and technical documentation using industry-standard design tools. Troubleshoot and repair complex electrical and electronic issues on ROV/AUV systems, including fiber optic systems, telemetry, high-voltage AC/DC distribution, and underwater communication links, both in the shop and during offshore operations. Support system integration, testing, and upgrades in collaboration with mechanical, software, and operations personnel. Assist with mobilization, demobilization, and offshore field support as required. Maintain detailed records of system configurations, repairs, modifications, and configuration control. Assist with development of technical procedures, work instructions, and safety protocols related to electrical systems. Provide technical input and documentation support for proposals, project planning, and customer deliverables as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree from an accredited college or university in Electrical Engineering, Electronics Engineering, Mechatronics, or a closely related field. Three (3) years of relevant experience in electrical system design, integration, and troubleshooting. Two (2) years of experience using electrical design tools (AutoCAD Electrical, Altium Designer, SolidWorks Electrical, or similar). US Citizen with a valid driver’s license required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Solid working knowledge of electrical engineering principles, circuit design, and component-level troubleshooting Ability to read, interpret, and create electrical schematics, wiring diagrams, and technical manuals Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail in operational and field environments Ability to work effectively as part of a multidisciplinary team (mechanical, software, operations) Strong written and verbal communication skills Willingness to learn and adapt quickly in a hands-on, mission-driven environment Familiarity with ROV/AUV systems or harsh-environment electronics is highly desirable Ability and willingness to travel and support extended offshore or remote field deployments as needed Preferred Qualifications Four to five (4–5) years of relevant electrical engineering experience. One to two (1–2) years of hands-on ROV, AUV, or subsea vehicle electrical systems experience. Engineer-in-Training (EIT) certification, or eligibility to obtain EIT certification shortly after hire. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5509?c=usm": {
      "title": "Grant Specialist I - CRPE",
      "description": "Grant Specialist I - CRPE | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Grant Specialist I - CRPE Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5509 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Grant Specialist I - CRPE The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Grant Specialist I - CRPE. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division College of Education and Human Sciences Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 53,000.00 - 60,000.00 Pay Grade E11 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please provide a 1-page summary of your experience in teacher preparation and in special education. This Grant Specialist position will work primarily with the Registered Teacher Apprenticeship in Special Education initiative of REACH MS, the State Personnel Development Grant.  This person will coordinate and support the development of high-quality Special Education Registered Teacher Apprenticeship Programs by providing training, coaching, and technical assistance to educator preparation programs, districts, mentors, and workforce partners across the state of Mississippi. This is a grant-funded position and continued employment is contingent on grant funding. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Grant\nSpecialist I provides training, coaching, technical assistance, and\nimplementation support for state and federally funded grant initiatives.\nWorking under the direction of the Project Director, this position assists with\nimplementation of project activities by delivering evidence-based professional\nlearning, supporting implementation fidelity, collecting and utilizing data to\nguide continuous improvement, and collaborating with participating schools,\ndistricts, and project partners. The Grant Specialist I supports project\nimplementation, reporting, dissemination, and evaluation activities while\nensuring compliance with university, state, and federal grant requirements. The\nposition requires strong organizational skills, effective communication, collaboration\nwith diverse stakeholders, and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities\nwhile traveling extensively throughout the state. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Delivers evidence-based professional learning, technical assistance, coaching, and consultation to educators and other participants using established implementation frameworks, coaching models, and project procedures. Supports implementation of state and federally funded grant initiatives by assisting schools, districts, and partner organizations in implementing evidence-based practices with fidelity. Assists participants with collecting, analyzing, and utilizing implementation, fidelity, and outcome data to support continuous improvement and informed decision-making. Develops and maintains collaborative relationships with educators, administrators, families, community partners, and other project stakeholders and assists with the planning and coordination of meetings, trainings, conferences, and other project activities. Collects, organizes, and maintains project documentation, implementation records, participation data, and other required information and assists with preparing reports, presentations, dissemination materials, and grant deliverables. Completes assigned activities in accordance with project timelines and university, state, federal, and sponsor policies, procedures, and grant requirements and performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in education, special\neducation, behavioral sciences, psychology, counseling, social work, or a\nrelated field; two (2) years of experience providing educational, behavioral,\ninstructional, or related services in PK–12 educational settings; and a\ncurrent, valid Mississippi teaching license or eligibility to obtain\nMississippi teaching licensure within six (6) months of employment; OR Bachelor’s degree from an\naccredited college or university in a related field with either National Board\nCertification or evidence of substantial, recent, and relevant professional\nlearning, such as micro-credentials or certificate programs; five (5) years of\ndirectly related professional experience in PK–12 educational settings; and a\ncurrent, valid Mississippi teaching license or eligibility to obtain\nMississippi teaching licensure within six (6) months of employment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of evidence-based\n     instructional, behavioral, and implementation practices. Ability to develop and deliver\n     effective professional learning, coaching, and technical assistance. Strong written, verbal, and\n     interpersonal communication skills. Ability to establish and\n     maintain collaborative working relationships with educators,\n     administrators, community partners, and project stakeholders. Strong organizational, project\n     coordination, and time management skills. Ability to analyze\n     implementation and outcome data to support continuous improvement. Ability to work independently\n     while managing multiple priorities, deadlines, and travel schedules. Proficiency with Microsoft\n     Office applications, Google Workspace, learning management systems,\n     virtual meeting platforms, and other technology used to support grant\n     implementation. Preferred Qualifications Master’s\ndegree in special education, education, behavioral sciences, psychology,\ncounseling, social work, or a related field. Three (3) or more years of related\nexperience in PK–12 educational settings, including at least two (2) years\ndelivering professional learning, technical assistance, or coaching to\neducators. Experience implementing evidence-based educational or school\nimprovement initiatives, supporting state or federally funded grants, utilizing\nimplementation or outcome data for continuous improvement, and using\ninstructional technology to support professional learning. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5507?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Library and Information Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Library and Information Science | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor in Library and Information Science Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5507 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor in Library and Information Science The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor in Library and Information Science. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Library and Information Sciences Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 65,000.00 - 70,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date February 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for the position of Assistant Professor in the School of Library and Information Science. This tenure-track position comes with a 3/3 teaching load with opportunities for additional compensation through summer teaching. The successful candidate will teach synchronous courses, conduct research, and participate in service to the profession and University. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Ideal candidates will have a robust research agenda that complements the existing strengths of the faculty. In addition, we seek applicants who have the ability to teach a variety of courses in emerging information science areas, such as data science, informatics and artificial intelligence, as well as courses in librarianship, including cataloging, collection development, and reference. Primary job duties include: The ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students from diverse backgrounds. Conducting an active research agenda through publication in journals and participation in scholarly conferences. The ability to teach in the core curriculum as well as develop new course offerings in the candidate’s area of specialization. Support University and School activities through service and membership in professional organizations. Support undergraduate and graduate students through regular advising and mentorship. Follow School and University policies and perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications A Master’s degree in Library and Information Science and a\nDoctoral degree in Library and Information Science or related field from an\naccredited college or university is required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to teach synchronously online Excellent written and oral communication skills and the ability to communicate with a diverse group of individuals Excellent organization and time management skills Familiarity with current LMS platforms (preferably Canvas) Evidence of a current or emerging research agenda related to a library and information science topic Ability to teach evenings Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching online and prior work experience in a professional information setting (i.e. library, archive, museum, etc.) is desired. Ongoing demonstrated scholarship, including but not limited to, prior successful grant submissions and publication in peer-reviewed journals is ideal. Individuals with a strong record of teaching and scholarship situated within information science topics including data management, informatics, and artificial intelligence/technology are strongly preferred. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5499?c=usm": {
      "title": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Experimental)",
      "description": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Experimental) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Experimental) Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5499 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Experimental) The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Experimental). Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Psychology Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 1st but we welcome applications anytime and will continue to review as received until the position is filled . Contact Dr. Kenji Noguchi ( kenji . noguchi @usm.edu) to inquire about the position. A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) names and contact information for three references (reference letters will be solicited at a later stage of the application process upon request), 4) academic transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable), 5) a research statement (1-2 pages) describing the applicant's program of research and impact, and 6) a teaching statement (1-2 pages) describing the applicant’s teaching philosophy, experiences, and approach. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Psychology at the University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for one, full-time, tenure track, 9-month, Assistant Professor position beginning August 2027. This is an exciting opportunity to join a diverse experimental psychology doctoral program in the School of Psychology. The Experimental program is one of four doctoral programs in the School of Psychology. The Experimental doctoral program offers generalist training in research-based approaches to Psychology in several different research areas. The research area of specialization for this position is open . W e are interested in candidates whose training backgrounds complement or enhance our current concentrations, i ncluding but not limited to expertise in memory, perception, social psychology, developmental psychology, and behavioral neuroscience . The Experimental Psychology doctoral program emphasizes research mentorship, diversity, and undergraduate and graduate teaching. Our faculty have established records of scholarship in the areas of memory, aging and cognition, sensation and perception, evolutionary psychology, health psychology, and social psychology. We aim to recruit applicants who will produce impactful research with the potential to secure extramural funding, and who will emphasize training doctoral students to become productive and thoughtful scientists. The School of Psychology has approximately 600 undergraduate majors and 125 graduate students across three APA-accredited doctoral programs (Counseling, Clinical, & School), a doctoral program in Experimental Psychology and a MPCAC accredited Master’s program in Counseling Psychology. Qualified applicants will be prepared to contribute to the teaching mission of the School of Psychology at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. More information can be found at www.usm.edu/graduate-programs/psychology- experimental .php. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop and maintain a strong\nprogram of research. Teach a combination of\nundergraduate and graduate classes. Seek\nextramural funding. Contribute\nto the mission of the university and profession through service\nactivities. Perform\nother duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications include a doctoral degree from an accredited college or university in experimental psychology or related fields (by August 2027). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exceptional written and oral communication and interpersonal skills. Proven track record of innovative teaching practices and the ability to teach effectively at the university level in an undergraduate and graduate psychology program. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and collegially with students, staff, and faculty from diverse backgrounds, programs, and colleges. Knowledge of the field of Psychology and associated research methodologies, teaching, and scholarly tools. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of, or potential for, conducting research, obtaining extramural funding, and high-quality teaching and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5498?c=usm": {
      "title": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Clinical)",
      "description": "Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Clinical) | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Clinical) Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5498 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Clinical) The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Psychology, Tenure Track Assistant Professor (Clinical). Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Psychology Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 1st but we welcome applications anytime and will continue to review as received until the position is filled . Contact Dr. Emily Junkin (emily.junkin@usm.edu) to inquire about the position even if the initial review date has passed. A completed application will include 1) a cover letter describing strengths and qualifications for the position, 2) a CV, 3) names and contact information for three references (reference letters will be solicited at a later stage of the application process upon request), 4) academic transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable to expedite initial review; official transcripts will be expected prior to campus interview), 5) a research statement (1-2 pages) describing the applicant's program of research and impact, and 6) a teaching statement (1-2 pages) describing the applicant’s teaching philosophy, experiences, and approach. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Psychology at the University of Southern Mississippi (USM) invites applicants for two full-time, tenure-track, Assistant Professor positions beginning August 2027. This is an exciting opportunity to join a dynamic scientist-practitioner, APA-accredited Clinical Psychology doctoral training program in the School of Psychology. The Clinical Psychology program emphasizes research mentorship and training in evidence-based practices, and our faculty value collegiality and a collaborative, supportive work environment. We offer training concentrations in child and adult clinical psychology. Research and applied interests are open; we are interested in considering applicants who can contribute to either adult or child concentrations. Our faculty have established records of scholarship in neurodevelopmental disorders, clinical health psychology, alcohol and other drug use, identity and mental health disparities, trauma and adversity, neuropsychological assessment, measurement development, and child/adolescent externalizing behavior. We seek applicants who are eager to advance their program of research and provide high-quality research mentorship to graduate students. Southern Miss offers exceptional institutional support and college-level assistance in securing external funding, and faculty research benefits from access to a large undergraduate research participation pool. Our doctoral students provide psychological services through the Center for Behavioral Health (CBH) , which is an integrated in-house training clinic staffed by students and faculty from the School, Counseling, and Clinical Psychology training programs. The CBH offers assessment and treatment services to diverse clientele from the community and allows for close supervision of student clinicians by program faculty, supported by the CBH’s state-of-the-art video system. Student clinicians also receive supervised experience serving community clients in a range of external practicum placements (e.g., acute inpatient unit, VA hospitals, medical centers, serious mental illness specialty program, juvenile justice, child advocacy center, schools, private practice). We hope to recruit applicants interested in providing clinical supervision of practicum students in our in-house training clinic. Though not requiring postdoctoral hours, opportunities for peer supervision during the licensure process in Mississippi (including mentorship, professional development) are available from licensed faculty. Additional research mentoring is available through the tenure and promotion process. The Clinical Psychology program is one of four doctoral programs in the School of Psychology. The School of Psychology has approximately 600 undergraduate majors and 125 graduate students across three APA-accredited doctoral programs (Counseling, Clinical, & School), a doctoral program in Experimental Psychology and an MPCAC-accredited Master’s program in Counseling Psychology. Qualified applicants will be prepared to contribute to the teaching mission of the School of Psychology at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Faculty have ample opportunities for professional development in teaching, mentoring, scholarship, and leadership through the University’s Center for Faculty Development . Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develop and maintain a robust program of research. Teach undergraduate and graduate classes including graduate level practicum courses involving the clinical supervision of students in our in-house training clinic. Obtain licensure in the state of Mississippi (note that MS does not require postdoctoral hours). Seek extramural funding. Contribute to the mission of the university and profession through service activities. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications include a doctoral degree in clinical psychology or related fields (by August 2027) and completion of an APA-accredited predoctoral internship. Applicants must be eligible for licensure as a psychologist in the State of Mississippi. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Exceptional written and oral communication and interpersonal skills. Proven track record of innovative teaching practices and the ability to teach effectively at the university level in an undergraduate and graduate psychology program. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and collegially with students, staff, and faculty from all backgrounds, programs, and colleges. Knowledge of the field of Psychology and associated research methodologies, teaching, and scholarly tools. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of, or potential for, conducting research, obtaining extramural funding, and high-quality teaching and mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5496?c=usm": {
      "title": "Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer",
      "description": "Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer Gulfport, MS, United States | req5496 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 70,536.00 - 95,432.00 Pay Grade E14 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Sensor Physics and Signal Processing Engineer conducts engineering\nand applied physics research involving the development, implementation, and\nevaluation of signal processing techniques and physics-based sensing methods\nfor autonomous underwater systems. The position develops and evaluates\nacoustic, magnetic, and other sensing algorithms; characterizes sensor\nperformance; and investigates the effects of environmental and operational\nconditions on sensing capabilities. Working collaboratively with multidisciplinary\nresearch and engineering teams, the position supports the development, testing,\nand transition of advanced sensing technologies that improve autonomous\nperception and decision-making at the Center for Ocean Enterprise. Primary\nJob Duties and Responsibilities Develops, implements, and evaluates signal processing algorithms for acoustic, magnetic, and other underwater sensing systems. Characterizes sensor performance and evaluates the effects of environmental and operational conditions on sensing capability, data quality, and detection performance. Develops detection, filtering, feature extraction, and sensor characterization techniques to support autonomous underwater sensing and perception. Collaborates with AI/ML, software, autonomy, and systems engineering researchers to integrate sensing algorithms into edge-deployable autonomous systems. Supports laboratory integration, simulation, pool testing, and open-water demonstrations involving autonomous underwater vehicles and advanced sensor payloads. Evaluates sensor performance through laboratory experiments, field-collected datasets, simulations, and modeling tools and documents findings through technical reports, publications, and presentations. Translates research findings into operational capabilities through the development, validation, and transition of sensing technologies for intelligent autonomous systems. Maintains knowledge of advances in underwater sensing, signal processing, and applied sensor physics and applies emerging methods to improve sensing performance in operational environments. Minimum Qualifications Master’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in Applied Physics, Physics,\nGeophysics, Remote Sensing, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field\nand six (6) years of related experience; or a Ph.D. from an accredited college\nor university in Applied Physics, Physics, Geophysics, Remote Sensing,\nElectrical Engineering, or a closely related field and four (4) years of\nrelated experience. Experience in signal processing, sensor characterization,\nphysics-based sensing, or related research. U.S. Citizenship with the ability\nto obtain a government security clearance. Valid driver’s license and\neligibility to obtain a Transportation Worker Identification Credential (TWIC). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA) Knowledge of signal processing principles and their application to acoustic, magnetic, and other sensing systems. Knowledge of physical principles governing underwater sensing systems and the effects of environmental and operational conditions on sensor performance. Knowledge of detection, filtering, feature extraction, sensor characterization, and performance evaluation techniques. Skill in developing, implementing, and evaluating signal processing and sensing algorithms. Skill in processing, analyzing, and interpreting large scientific and sensor datasets. Skill in scientific programming using Python, C/C++, or comparable programming languages and analysis tools. Ability to design and support laboratory experiments, simulations, and field testing of sensing systems. Ability to evaluate sensing system performance and translate scientific findings into practical engineering and operational solutions. Ability to interpret and apply scientific literature and emerging research methods. Ability to collaborate effectively with multidisciplinary teams, including AI/ML, software, autonomy, and systems engineering researchers. Ability to prepare technical reports, research publications, presentations, and other scientific documentation. Ability to work independently, manage multiple research priorities, and contribute effectively within a collaborative research environment. Preferred\nQualifications Experience\nwith acoustic, magnetic, or other underwater sensing systems and signal\nprocessing techniques for sonar, radar, lidar, or related sensing applications.\nExperience evaluating the effects of environmental and operational conditions\non sensor performance and applying sensor characterization techniques.\nProficiency with Python, C/C++, or comparable scientific programming languages.\nContributions to applied research, technical reports, conference presentations,\nor peer-reviewed publications in signal processing, sensor physics, autonomous\nsystems, or a related field preferred. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5495?c=usm": {
      "title": "Geophysical Oceanographer",
      "description": "Geophysical Oceanographer | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Geophysical Oceanographer Gulfport, MS, United States | req5495 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 9/2/2026 Back to Search Geophysical Oceanographer The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Geophysical Oceanographer. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 70,536.00 - 95,432.00 Pay Grade E14 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This position conducts applied oceanographic and geophysical research\nsupporting autonomous underwater systems, seabed characterization, multi-sensor\ndata collection, and environmental context modeling. The position plans and\nanalyzes underwater survey data, characterizes seafloor and environmental\nconditions, and evaluates their impact on survey quality, sensor\ninterpretation, and autonomous mission planning. Working collaboratively with\nAI/ML engineers, signal processing researchers, and field operations personnel,\nthe position supports the research, development, testing, and evaluation of\nadvanced underwater sensing and autonomous systems at the Center for Ocean\nEnterprise. Primary\nJob Duties and Responsibilities Conducts geophysical and oceanographic characterization for autonomous underwater sensing, including analysis and interpretation of seabed, bathymetric, environmental, sonar, magnetic, navigation, and other geospatial survey data. Plans, supports, and evaluates multi-sensor underwater data collection involving side-scan sonar, synthetic aperture sonar, multibeam echosounders, magnetometers, ROVs, navigation systems, and environmental sensors. Defines and evaluates environmental, seabed, and survey metadata needed to support AI/ML, signal processing, sensor interpretation, and autonomy workflows, including bottom type, bathymetry, acoustic context, navigation quality, survey quality, and sensor operating conditions. Evaluates the effects of seabed characteristics, environmental conditions, sensor geometry, vehicle motion, altitude, range, and survey design on data quality, sensor performance, interpretability, and model confidence. Develops and evaluates data quality standards and environmentally informed decision-support approaches for underwater survey products, translating oceanographic and geophysical conditions into model inputs, performance metrics, confidence factors, and operational guidance. Interprets georeferenced sonar, bathymetric, magnetic, ROV, and related datasets to support seabed classification, environmental characterization, reacquisition planning, and validation of autonomous perception and sensing outputs. Collaborates with AI/ML, signal processing, software, sensor engineering, and field operations personnel to incorporate real-world oceanographic and seabed conditions into model development, performance evaluation, testing, and mission planning. Prepares technical reports, maps, data summaries, survey assessments, research publications, presentations, and other documentation; remains current with advances in geophysical oceanography, hydrographic surveying, marine remote sensing, seabed classification, and autonomous underwater sensing. Minimum Qualifications Master’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in Geophysical Oceanography,\nPhysical Oceanography, Geophysics, Hydrography, or a related field and six (6)\nyears of related experience; or a Ph.D. from an accredited college or\nuniversity in Geophysical Oceanography, Physical Oceanography, Geophysics,\nHydrography, or a related field and four (4) years of related experience. U.S.\nCitizenship with the ability to obtain a government security clearance. Valid\ndriver’s license and eligibility to obtain a Transportation Worker\nIdentification Credential (TWIC). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities (KSA) Knowledge of geophysical\n     oceanography, seabed characterization, hydrographic surveying, and/or\n     marine remote sensing principles and practices. Knowledge of underwater survey\n     data interpretation, including sonar imagery, bathymetry, navigation, and\n     geospatial data. Knowledge of the effects of\n     seabed characteristics, water-column conditions, sensor geometry, survey\n     design, and operational conditions on underwater sensing and data quality. Knowledge of environmental and\n     geophysical metadata used in AI/ML, signal processing, sensor\n     interpretation, and autonomous systems. Knowledge of underwater sensing\n     technologies, including side-scan sonar, synthetic aperture sonar,\n     multibeam echosounders, magnetometers, ROVs, and related systems. Skill in analyzing and\n     evaluating large geospatial, oceanographic, acoustic, bathymetric, and\n     remote-sensing datasets. Skill in evaluating underwater\n     survey quality, including resolution, coverage, navigation consistency,\n     altitude, range, motion effects, acoustic artifacts, and georeferencing. Ability to translate scientific,\n     environmental, and geophysical information into engineering, testing,\n     performance assessment, and operational guidance. Ability to collaborate\n     effectively with multidisciplinary teams, including AI/ML, software,\n     signal processing, sensor engineering, and field operations personnel. Ability to communicate complex\n     scientific and technical information effectively through technical\n     reports, publications, maps, briefings, presentations, and other research\n     documentation. Ability to work independently,\n     manage multiple research priorities, and coordinate research and\n     field-support activities in a collaborative environment. Preferred\nQualifications Experience\nwith autonomous underwater vehicles, unmanned maritime systems, or field-based\noceanographic operations; underwater sensor data collection and analysis;\nseabed classification, sediment characterization, or acoustic interpretation;\nand evaluating the effects of environmental conditions on survey quality and\nsensor performance. Experience developing marine survey or test plans,\nquality-control procedures, and working with geospatial or environmental data.\nContributions to applied research, technical reports, peer-reviewed\npublications, or related field programs preferred. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5518?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, School of Accountancy",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, School of Accountancy | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Professor, School of Accountancy Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5518 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/31/2026 Back to Search Assistant Professor, School of Accountancy The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Professor, School of Accountancy. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Accountancy Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Complete applications received by 5:00 PM MST on Friday, November 15, 2026, will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until filled. Applications submitted through email or surface mail will\nnot be considered. Applicants must apply at https://jobs.usm.edu to be\nconsidered. The following are required for your application to be complete and\nto be considered: 1) a cover letter that describes the candidate’s\nqualifications for the position as detailed in this announcement; 2) a current\ncurriculum vitae; 3) evidence of teaching effectiveness, if applicable (e.g., a\nsample of recent, system-generated teaching evaluations); 4) evidence of\nscholarship in the form of recent publication(s) or working paper(s); and 5)\nnames and contact information for three professional references, at least two\nof whom can provide an evaluation of teaching and research ability or potential. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The University of Southern Mississippi invites applicants\nfor a full-time, nine-month tenure-track faculty position in the School of\nAccountancy to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will primarily\nteach undergraduate and graduate courses in financial or cost/managerial\naccounting, with possible teaching duties in tax as needed. The candidate will\nbe required to teach at the Hattiesburg campus and online/hybrid courses using\nvarious forms of technology. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Research\n     duties and responsibilities will include publishing in highly-rated\n     accounting journals. School of Accountancy faculty are actively engaged in\n     scholarly, professional, and pedagogical research to extend the knowledge\n     boundaries of the accounting discipline while maintaining the currency of\n     their academic/professional qualifications and the school’s curriculum. Duties\n     and responsibilities of this position include excellence in teaching undergraduate\n     and graduate courses in accounting and service to the School of\n     Accountancy, College of Business and Economic Development, university, and\n     the academy. Teaching duties will be in our bachelor’s in accounting,\n     Master of Professional Accountancy, and/or Master of Business\n     Administration programs based on need. The individual will be assigned to\n     teach undergraduate and graduate courses either in financial or\n     cost/managerial accounting. The individual hired may also be required to\n     teach one or more courses in taxation as a secondary area of teaching.\n     Classes in other areas will be assigned as needed and efforts will be made\n     to find opportunities for the faculty member to teach in his/her special\n     areas of expertise. Classes may be on-campus, online, or hybrid. The\n     individual selected must demonstrate a collegial and team-oriented\n     approach to research, teaching, and service. In addition to excelling in research,\n     the successful candidate must be devoted to teaching excellence at the\n     graduate and undergraduate levels and must demonstrate a commitment to\n     student success. All faculty are also required to be actively engaged in\n     our assurance of learning processes. The\n     School of Accountancy holds separate AACSB accreditation. All faculty in\n     the school are required to contribute to the maintenance of separate AACSB\n     accreditation. Performs\n     other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (or ABD*) in Accounting or other appropriate related field from an AACSB accredited institution. Meet the requirements of a scholarly academic in accounting for AACSB accreditation purposes. For \ncandidates with prior employment in higher education, evidence of \nexcellence in collegiate teaching and institutional/professional service\n is required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to teach effectively (both online and in traditional settings) at the university level. Exceptional written and\noral communication and interpersonal skills. Proven track record of\ninnovative teaching practices and research impact. Demonstrated ability to work effectively and collegially with students, staff, and faculty from diverse backgrounds, programs, and colleges. Knowledge of the field of accounting and taxation. The ability to navigate and use learning management systems for teaching, such as Canvas, as well as other technological communications (Microsoft Office Suite). Proficiency in teaching strategies and techniques for diverse student populations. Preferred Qualifications Experience in public or corporate accounting or taxation. Professional certification (CPA, CMA, licensed attorney, etc.). Experience in teaching hybrid/flipped/online classes. Evidence of potential for excellence in scholarly research. *ABD\napplicants must have completed all doctoral course requirements and qualifying\nexams and must persuasively demonstrate that all degree requirements will be\ncompleted before the start of the position. The School of Accountancy The School of Accountancy is separately accredited by\nAACSB and offers undergraduate and master degrees with an extensive network of\nalumni in local, state, and federal service. The Hattiesburg area has an\nestimated population of approximately 150,000 and is one of the fastest growing\nregions in the State of Mississippi. The main campus is located in the\nculturally diverse and economically dynamic southern part of Mississippi about\n65 miles from the Gulf Coast. Students, faculty and staff benefit from a climate\nthat fosters year-round outdoor activities, and the quality of life is\ncharacterized by a reasonable cost of living coupled with easy access to major\nmetropolitan areas such as New Orleans, LA; Mobile, AL; and Jackson, MS. You\ncan find further information on the School of Accountancy at https://www.usm.edu/accountancy/. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5500?c=usm": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Staff",
      "description": "Campus Safety Staff | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Campus Safety Staff Ocean Springs, MS, United States | req5500 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 8/27/2026 Back to Search Campus Safety Staff The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Campus Safety Staff. Position Details Location Gulf Coast Research Laboratory 703 East Beach Drive Ocean Springs, Mississippi, 39564 United States Division GCRL University Police Department Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade N03 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Campus Safety Staff secures assigned\nUniversity Academic and Administrative Buildings. The Campus Safety Staff\nmaintains a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, and staff by\nconducting security checks in assigned areas to include Academic Building,\nAdministrative Buildings, Parking Lots, Residential Buildings and reports\nsuspicious activities to University Dispatch/UPD when needed, ensures\ncompliance with University and Residence Life policies and responds immediately\nto emergency situations, i.e. fire alarms, security alarms, and medical/injury\ncalls. Primary Duties and Responsibilities The University Police Secures\n     University Academic and Administrative Buildings. Conducts frequent patrols\n     of assigned area for the purpose of detecting and reporting suspicious\n     behavior and/or activity. Monitors Residence Hall\n     entrances for any unauthorized entries. Monitors Residence Hall\n     entrances for any unauthorized entries. Provides authorized\n     safety escorts to members of the campus community. Interacts with campus\n     visitors while assisting with directions and/or other information. Performs other duties as\n     assigned to accomplish the goals of Department. Minimum Qualifications High\nSchool Diploma and/or General Equivalency Diploma (G.E.D). One\nto three months of related or equivalent combination of education and\nexperience. Mississippi\nDriver’s License Knowledge,\nSkills, and Abilities (KSA) Knowledge\nand skill within Windows-based computer and software applications, to include\nMicrosoft Office applications. Ability to use email to send and receive\ncorrespondence. Strong oral, written, and interpersonal communication and\ninterpersonal skills. Ability to establish and maintain cooperative working\nrelationships and to interact with students, faculty and staff. Preferred Qualifications Three\nyears of experience as a security/safety professional. Experience responding to\nemergencies. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
