    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5447?c=usm": {
      "title": "Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporter, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center",
      "description": "Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporter, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporter, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5447 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/27/2026 Back to Search Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporter, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporter, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Journalism, Public Relations, and Advertising Position Type Staff Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 12.00 - 12.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Roy Howard Community Journalism Center is seeking motivated high school and community college students to serve as Southeast Mississippi Planner (SMP) Reporters. SMP Reporters help maintain one of Mississippi’s most comprehensive community news and events calendars by researching, verifying, writing, and publishing civic information that connects residents with opportunities throughout Southeast Mississippi. Working alongside professional journalists and university student leaders, SMP Reporters develop practical newsroom skills through community information reporting—the process of identifying, verifying, and publishing timely, accurate information that helps residents stay informed and engaged. Students gain hands-on experience in reporting, interviewing, AP-style writing, digital publishing, audience engagement, and community journalism while covering community events, government meetings, nonprofit organizations, educational opportunities, festivals, and other civic happenings. This position is designed for high school juniors and seniors and community college students interested in journalism, communication, writing, public affairs, digital media, or related fields. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Research, verify, write, and publish community events and civic information for the Southeast Mississippi Planner. Contact organizations, government agencies, schools, businesses, and nonprofits to gather and confirm event information. Write clear, concise, and engaging stories following AP Style and RHCJC standards. Conduct interviews and background research when developing stories or expanded community coverage. Monitor community websites, agendas, newsletters, press releases, and social media to identify newsworthy events and updates. Capture photographs and basic video content when appropriate to enhance Planner coverage. Collaborate with professional staff and fellow student journalists to identify underserved communities and expand Planner coverage. Represent the Roy Howard Community Journalism Center professionally during community events and outreach activities. Participate in editorial meetings, training sessions, and professional development opportunities. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Current or incoming high school junior or senior or currently enrolled at a community college. GPA of 2.0 or higher. Valid Mississippi driver’s license or reliable transportation. Strong writing and communication skills. Interest in journalism, community engagement, writing, or public service. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong writing, grammar, spelling, and editing skills. Ability to research, organize, and verify information accurately. Excellent attention to detail. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to communicate professionally with community organizations and public officials. Ability to manage multiple assignments and meet deadlines. Familiarity with social media platforms and digital communication. Ability to learn new technology and newsroom software quickly. Self-motivated, dependable, and receptive to coaching and feedback. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team. Preferred Qualifications Experience with school newspapers, yearbook, broadcast journalism, digital media, or other student publications. Familiarity with AP Style. Experience with photography, videography, or social media. Portfolio of writing samples or school projects. Letter of recommendation from a teacher, advisor, or faculty member. Essay describing interest in community journalism and career goals. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5446?c=usm": {
      "title": "Multimedia Journalism Internship, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center",
      "description": "Multimedia Journalism Internship, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Multimedia Journalism Internship, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5446 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/27/2026 Back to Search Multimedia Journalism Internship, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Multimedia Journalism Internship, Roy Howard Community Journalism Center. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Journalism, Public Relations, and Advertising Position Type Staff Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 12.00 - 12.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Roy Howard Community Journalism Center (RHCJC) is seeking motivated college students for a paid Multimedia Journalism Internship. This hands-on opportunity provides real-world experience in reporting, photography, videography, digital storytelling, social media, and audience engagement while serving communities across Southeast Mississippi. Interns will work alongside professional journalists to create impactful multimedia content, support community engagement initiatives, and gain practical newsroom experience in a collaborative environment. This internship is open to students currently enrolled at colleges and universities outside the University of Southern Mississippi who are interested in journalism, communication, media production, photography, videography, digital media, strategic communication, marketing, public relations, or related fields. Internship opportunities are available at our Hattiesburg, Long Beach, and Jackson locations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Research, report, write, photograph, and/or produce multimedia stories that inform and engage local communities. Capture and edit photography and video content for digital, broadcast, and social media platforms. Create digital content for websites, newsletters, social media, and other audience engagement initiatives. Assist with social media content creation,\n     scheduling, audience interaction, and performance monitoring. Conduct interviews and gather information from community members, local leaders, and subject matter experts. Collaborate with RHCJC staff, student employees, and other interns on multimedia storytelling projects. Support community engagement events, media literacy programs, town halls, and other public outreach initiatives. Adhere to professional journalism standards, including accuracy, fairness, ethical reporting, fact-checking, and verification. Participate in editorial meetings, planning sessions, and professional development opportunities. Represent the Roy Howard Community Journalism Center professionally during field assignments, community events, and partner activities. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Currently\n enrolled at a college or university other than the University of \nSouthern Mississippi pursuing a degree in journalism, communication, \ndigital media, public relations, marketing, media production, or a \nrelated field. Strong interest in multimedia storytelling, community journalism, digital content creation, or audience engagement. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a team environment. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong writing, storytelling, and communication skills. Ability to produce engaging multimedia content across multiple platforms Knowledge of journalism ethics and commitment to accuracy. Understanding of social media platforms, audience engagement, and digital best practices. Ability to conduct interviews and build relationships with diverse community members. Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple assignments and deadlines. Ability to work collaboratively in a fast-paced newsroom environment. Willingness to learn new technologies, storytelling techniques, and digital tools. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience with student media, internships, freelance work, or organizational communications. Experience with photography, videography, social media management, graphic design, or multimedia production. Familiarity with AP Style and Adobe Creative Suite (Photoshop, Premiere Pro, Audition, InDesign) or similar software. Experience with Canva, social media scheduling platforms, or digital analytics tools. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5448?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct, School of Management",
      "description": "Adjunct, School of Management | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct, School of Management Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5448 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/23/2026 Back to Search Adjunct, School of Management The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct, School of Management. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Management Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants The School of Management accepts applications for Adjunct Faculty on an ongoing, rolling basis. We continuously review submissions to maintain a qualified pool of instructors for our courses in Entrepreneurship, Human Resources, Management, Operations Management, and Strategy . Because adjunct roles provide flexible, as-needed support for both in-person and online courses, this active requisition allows us to respond rapidly to shifting enrollment or emergency staffing needs. To be considered, please ensure your application includes: Cover Letter : Explicitly state your preferred teaching modalities and locations (Hattiesburg Campus, Long Beach/Gulf Park Campus, and/or Online). Curriculum Vitae (CV) Unofficial Transcripts : Highlighting your graduate-level management coursework. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Adjunct faculty members serve as the Instructor of Record, delivering high-quality course instruction across face-to-face, hybrid, and/or online modalities, including all aspects of course development and administration. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Deliver\n     face-to-face, hybrid, and online classes in strict adherence to posted\n     academic schedules. Clearly\n     communicate course requirements, grading rubrics, and expectations to\n     students. Maintain\n     availability for student academic support, advising, exams, remediation,\n     and evaluations. Collaborate\n     with College of Business and Economic Development (CBED) faculty and the\n     School Director to align course offerings with institutional quality\n     metrics. Adhere\n     to all established policies, procedures, and ethical standards of CBED and\n     the University of Southern Mississippi. Perform\n     administrative and instructional tasks as assigned by the Director. Minimum Qualifications A\n     master’s degree in a related field from a regionally accredited\n     institution. A\n     minimum of 18 graduate credit hours in a management discipline from\n     an accredited business school (AACSB, ACBSP, or IACBE). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated\n     professional work or teaching experience in management. Strong\n     verbal and written communication skills with a focus on timely student\n     feedback. Ability\n     to work collaboratively with diverse faculty within the School of\n     Management. Proficiency\n     with Learning Management Systems (specifically Canvas) and standard\n     productivity software (Microsoft Office Suite). Knowledge\n     of inclusive teaching strategies tailored to diverse student populations. Preferred Qualifications An\n     earned doctorate (Ph.D. or D.B.A.) in a management discipline from an\n     AACSB-accredited program. Substantial\n     executive or professional leadership experience in a management field. Documented\n     history of successful online/hybrid/flipped classroom instruction and\n     Canvas certification. Active\n     scholarly research or recognized professional certifications (e.g.,\n     SHRM-CP, PMP). About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5432?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Athletic Training",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Athletic Training | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Instructor - Athletic Training Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5432 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor - Athletic Training The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct Instructor - Athletic Training. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Health Professions Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants\nshould include: Cover letter summarizing academic preparation and professional experience Curriculum vitae / Resume Official transcripts from all educational institutions Proof of Mississippi athletic training licensure (if licensed at time of application) Applications\nfor Adjunct Faculty will be accepted on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed\nas needed. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This part-time adjunct faculty position requires teaching in-person undergraduate courses in the Athletic Training degree program on an as needed basis. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Face-to-face and/or online course delivery and instruction. Prepare and submit syllabi, grades and other required course documentation in a timely manner. Communicate course requirements and expectations to students. Communicate with other program and school-level faculty. Performs other duties, as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's Degree or higher in Athletic Training or a related field Mississippi state license or eligible Ability to teach effectively, according to University standards, in the undergraduate and graduate Athletic Training programs Criminal history and background check clearance Uphold the mission and values of USM, College of Nursing and Health Professions, and the School of Health Professions Knowledge,\nSkills, and Abilities (KSA) Specialized knowledge in the field of Athletic Training as demonstrated by national certification. Candidates should have the ability to deliver accurate, concise and quality communication (verbal and written) in a timely manner. Candidates should have the ability to work collaboratively on interdisciplinary teams. Candidates should have the ability to navigate and use learning management systems for teaching, such as Canvas, as well as other technological communications (Microsoft Office Suite). Preferred Qualifications Teaching, mentoring, and/or service experience at the university level. Professional experience in Athletic Training. Experience with USM's Learning Management System, Canvas. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5431?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Mathematics",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty Mathematics | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Faculty Mathematics Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5431 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Faculty Mathematics The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty Mathematics. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Mathematics and Natural Sciences Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a Cover Letter, a current Curriculum Vitae, and a list of names and contact information for three professional references. When applying for part-time adjunct faculty, you are submitting your application to the School of Mathematics and Natural Sciences adjunct faculty pool. We will accept applications on a continuing basis. There may or may not be a hiring need at this time in your area of interest. The program coordinators access the applicant pool when there is a hiring need. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Mathematics and Natural Sciences at the University of Southern Mississippi invites applications to establish a pool of qualified applicants for current and future part-time Adjunct Faculty appointments (online and/or face-to-face). Successful applicants may teach up to six semester credit hours (2 courses per semester) of undergraduate mathematics courses, delivered online and/or face-to-face on our Hattiesburg, Mississippi campus. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach assigned undergraduate courses, including: Preparing course syllabus, lectures, assignments, and other course components as necessary. Using Canvas to manage the course. Utilizing effective teaching methods to ensure that all course outcomes are met. Timely evaluation of student work with constructive feedback, and assignment of grades. Being available to students for Q&A. Submission of course assessments to the Program Coordinator for accreditation purposes. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree ( or 18 hours of graduate course work) in Mathematics or Mathematics Education from an accredited university Knowledge\n of undergraduate mathematics, including College Algebra, Trigonometry, \nCalculus, Differential Equations, Linear Algebra, Statistics, or other \nassigned courses. Knowledge of evidence-based instructional strategies and best practices in mathematics education. Ability to teach effectively (both online and in tradtional settings) at the university level. Background Check Clearance Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Ability to teach undergraduate-level courses and clearly communicate technical content to all student populations. Skill in preparing course materials, assessing student performance, and using instructional technologies effectively. Ability to integrate practical, industry-based examples into instruction to support applied learning. Ability to collaborate with faculty and staff while maintaining academic standards and complying with university policies. Preferred Qualifications Previous college level teaching experience. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills. Experience with online course delivery and instruction. Experience with Canvas technology. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5429?c=usm": {
      "title": "VORTEX-SE Community Engagement Specialist",
      "description": "VORTEX-SE Community Engagement Specialist | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) VORTEX-SE Community Engagement Specialist Ocean Springs, MS, United States | req5429 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/21/2026 Back to Search VORTEX-SE Community Engagement Specialist The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of VORTEX-SE Community Engagement Specialist. Position Details Location Gulf Coast Research Laboratory 703 East Beach Drive Ocean Springs, Mississippi, 39564 United States Division Mississippi-Alabama Sea Grant Consortium Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 60,000.00 - 75,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). The National Severe Storms Laboratory (NSSL) Verification of the Origins\nof Rotation in Tornadoes EXperiment-Southeast (VORTEX-SE) program has embedded\nsocial and behavioral science research into its program since its inception.\nSince 2016 VORTEX-SE research has examined societal vulnerability to tornado\nrisk, communication of these risks, and the roles of the National Weather\nService (NWS) and its partners in building local resilience to tornadoes.\nVORTEX-SE has been iterative in its approach so that new findings and knowledge\nare built into research going forward. The Mississippi-Alabama Sea Grant Consortium (MASGC) in collaboration\nwith NOAA’s National Severe Storms Laboratory (NSSL) have partnered to create a\nmodel for a regional extension program that will integrate physical and social\nscience research from the VORTEX-SE program to local application for a broader\ntarget audience. The goal of this regional effort is to support two-way dialog\nthat contributes to the understanding of on-the-ground needs of audiences that\nare vulnerable to severe weather events and directly respond to those needs\nwith accurate, trusted information delivered by extension specialists,\nresearchers, and other experts. Job Summary The VORTEX-SE Community\nEngagement Specialist serves as a regional liaison between VORTEX-SE scientists\nand the communities that rely on accurate and timely severe weather\ninformation. This position facilitates the exchange of knowledge by translating\nscientific research into practical outreach, education, and engagement\nactivities while also communicating community needs and priorities back to\nresearchers. The Specialist develops and delivers educational programs,\noutreach materials, workshops, and other engagement initiatives to support\ninformed decision-making and strengthen community resilience across the\nSoutheast. This position works collaboratively with VORTEX-SE scientists, the\nNational Severe Storms Laboratory (NSSL), the Mississippi-Alabama Sea Grant\nConsortium (MASGC), and regional stakeholders and requires extensive travel\nthroughout the Southeast. This is a grant-funded, limited-term appointment\ncontingent upon continued funding. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Work with the NSSL VORTEX Program Lead and VORTEX scientists to help synthesize and prioritize research results for transition and knowledge transfer to appropriate communities in the Southeast through the MASGC VORTEX-SE extension project. Develop and execute (through focus groups and workshops) extension programming grounded in VORTEX funded science and related research and the needs of target audiences and communities. Author 1-3 publications for non-technical audiences each year and participate in planning at least two workshops/trainings each year to share VORTEX research results within the geographic area (e.g. hosting science seminars and/or theme-based workshops). Contribute to other outreach activities supported by VORTEX such as social media, website(s), YouTube videos, newsletters, TV and radio segments, and other local, regional and national media reports where appropriate. Work with VORTEX Engagement Coordinator for regional consistency, coordination and synthesis of outreach products, conduct program evaluations and submission of annual reports. Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with emergency managers, local governments, building officials, extension professionals, community organizations, and other stakeholders throughout the region. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in emergency management,\nbuilding science, disaster management, building construction, or a related\nfield. Such education and/or experience should include three (3) years of\nprogressively responsible experience in community engagement, Extension,\noutreach, emergency management, science communication, or a related field. An\nequivalent combination of years of experience and education may be considered\nfor substitution of educational requirements (i.e. military experience). Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of community engagement, outreach, extension programming, or adult education principles, with the ability to develop, implement, and evaluate educational programs. Ability to interpret complex scientific or technical information and communicate it effectively to technical and non-technical audiences through written, verbal, and presentation formats. Strong project management, organizational, analytical, and planning skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and complete projects independently with minimal supervision. Excellent interpersonal skills with the ability to build collaborative relationships and work effectively with diverse stakeholders, partner organizations, and multidisciplinary teams. Proficiency with Microsoft Office Suite and other computer, communication, and virtual collaboration technologies. Ability to facilitate meetings, workshops, and public engagement activities while adapting to changing priorities and effectively managing multiple assignments. Ability to travel extensively throughout the Southeast region and work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Knowledge or experience in one or more relevant subject areas, such as severe weather awareness, disaster resilience, wind mitigation, building science, or related disciplines. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited college or\nuniversity in Emergency Management, Building Science, Disaster Management,\nBuilding Construction, Structural Engineering, Adult Education, or a closely\nrelated field. Preference will be given to candidates with demonstrated\nexperience in one or more of the following areas: emergency management,\nbuilding science, structural engineering, hazard identification and assessment,\nbuilding construction and code compliance, adult education, science\ncommunication, facilitation, curriculum development, public speaking,\nstakeholder engagement, or working with local, state, and federal government\nagencies. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5421?c=usm": {
      "title": "Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing",
      "description": "Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing Long Beach, MS, United States | req5421 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/8/2026 Back to Search Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing. Position Details Location Gulf Park 730 East Beach Boulevard Long Beach, Mississippi, 39560 United States Division College of Nursing GP Position Type Administrative Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 115,000.00 - 115,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date October 31, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Associate Director of Undergraduate Nursing provides administrative support to the Director of Nursing. The role is a 12-month position as the primary administrative point-of-contact and site director for all academic programs in the College of Nursing and Health Professions on the Gulf Park Campus. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Provides oversight of educational and administrative resources to assist with faculty concerns or issues related to those resources. Plans the orientation and mentorship of new full-time and adjunct faculty members. Monitors and reviews budgetary tracking for fiscally responsible decision-making at the School Director and college levels and subsequent approved budgetary processing. Manages course and clinical scheduling and textbook adoption. Assists with accreditation tracking and management. Responsible for clinical contract initiation, tracking, and management (in consultation with the Clinical Coordinators and Administrative Coordinators and Specialists). Monitors and evaluates clinical onboarding and student clearance for clinical participation at each facility (documentation of immunizations, TB, substance screen, CPR, etc.) Serves as Campus liaison for full-time and adjunct faculty member needs. Represents the College of Nursing and Health Professions at university and community events. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master of Science in Nursing (MSN) from an accredited institution required. Current, unencumbered Registered Nurse (RN) license. Minimum of five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in nursing education, including teaching, curriculum development, program evaluation, and/or academic administration. Demonstrated leadership or administrative experience supporting academic programs, faculty operations, or clinical education coordination. Minimum of two (2) years of clinical nursing practice. Experience with accreditation processes, regulatory compliance, and documentation management in nursing education. Experience in managing academic operations, including course scheduling, clinical placements, faculty support, and/or budget tracking. Ability to meet institutional requirements, including credential verification and background screening. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of day-to-day operations in the academic and clinical environment. Effective communication and interpersonal skills. Strong organizational and operational management skills. Strong problem-solving and decision-making skills in a fast-paced academic environment. Ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships. Ability to manage multiple priorities effectively while maintaining accuracy, organization, and adherence to deadlines. Preferred Qualifications Possesses a terminal degree in nursing (DNP or PhD) and has achieved a level of accomplishment in research, teaching, and service that merits appointment as an Associate Professor. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5409?c=usm": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor",
      "description": "Academic Advisor | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Academic Advisor Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5409 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 7/8/2026 Back to Search Academic Advisor The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Academic Advisor. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division College of Business and Economic Development Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade X06 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Advise undergraduate business students regarding progression to degree, course selections, and student success.  Assist the college with the recruitment and retention of students. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Advise continuing students each semester prior to registration; update the semester guide prior to the advising meeting. Evaluate transcripts and advise new prospective undergraduate and second degree students on the applicability of transfer credit for College of Business and Economic Development program requirements; prepare semester guides for new students showing courses completed; and meets individually with new students who missed Preview (orientation). Audit and approve applications for degree for undergraduate CBED students and meet with students when filing for degree to discuss GPA requirements; course requirements, residency requirements, and final-processing procedures. Advise and coach students on Probation, Probation Continued, and Suspension; hold signature authority for the Associate Dean for Undergraduate Education related to Exceptions in SOAR, Probation, Probation Continued, and Suspension student's SOAR holds. Answers questions from faculty, staff, and general public regarding degree requirements for CBED and College policies and University policies regarding enrollment; notifies faculty, staff, and students of important dates. Ensure student degree progress report is accurate in SOAR; process course substitutions in business core and general education core; process add/drop/withdrawal of classes, change of major/minor/certificate applications, overloads on classes and prerequisite for classes. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor's degree from an accredited college or university\nand one year of related experience and/or training. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of Microsoft Office Ability to occasionally travel or work nights/weekends Ability to effectively present information to small and large audiences Strong written communication skills, including email and postal correspondence, as well as reports and procedural manuals. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree from an accredited college or university;\nan educational background in business. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
