    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5382?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Social Work",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Social Work | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Instructor - Social Work Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5382 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/10/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor - Social Work The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct Instructor - Social Work. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Social Work Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date June 1, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants A\ncompleted application will include a copy of your current CV, transcript, and\nlicense (LMSW or LCSW). Official transcripts will be requested for selected applicants. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Adjunct\nfaculty members facilitate students' achievement of course objectives and\nprepare students to matriculate through the programs at the undergraduate and\ngraduate level. Prepare and submit syllabi, grades, and other required\ndocumentation in a timely manner. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Adhere to university policy and course schedule. Teach undergraduate and/or graduate coursework. Communicate any concerns with the appropriate program coordinator, director, or designee. Communicate course requirements to students. Provide accessible office hours to students. Report grades and other required documentation in a timely manner. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in Social Work from an accredited university. Two years post master's degree experience. Ability to teach effectively (both online and in traditional settings) at the university level in an undergraduate and graduate Social Work program. Uphold the mission and values of the School of Social Work. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Knowledge of the Social\n     Work Code of Ethics. Knowledge of Social\n     Work Professional and Technical Standards. Ability to develop\n     educational presentations on select topics. Ability to work as a part\n     of a team. Excellent written,\n     interpersonal, and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree in Social Work from an accredited university. License as an LCSW Teaching, mentoring, and service experience at the university level. Experience with online course delivery and instruction. Experience with Canvas and ZOOM technology. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5379?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor - Public Health",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor - Public Health | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Instructor - Public Health Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5379 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 6/9/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Instructor - Public Health The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct Instructor - Public Health. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division Public Health Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should include: Curriculum vitae / Resume Official transcripts from all educational institutions Applications for Adjunct Faculty will be accepted on an ongoing basis and will be reviewed as needed. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This part-time adjunct faculty position requires teaching in-person and/or online undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the Public Health degree program on an as needed basis. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Face-to-face course delivery and instruction. Prepare and submit syllabi, grades and other required course documentation in a timely manner. Communicate course requirements and expectations to students. Communicate with other program and school-level faculty. Performs other duties, as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Master's Degree or higher from an accredited college or university in Public Health or a related field. Ability to teach effectively, according to University standards, in the undergraduate and/or graduate Public Health programs. Criminal history and background check clearance. Uphold the mission and values of USM, College of Nursing and Health Professions, and the School of Health Professions. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Specialized knowledge in the field of Public Health as demonstrated by graduate level coursework or professional experience is required. Candidates\n should have the ability to deliver accurate, concise and quality \ncommunication (verbal and written) in a timely manner. Candidates should have the ability to work collaboratively on interdisciplinary teams. Candidates\n should have the ability to navigate and use learning management systems\n for teaching, such as Canvas, as well as other technological \ncommunications (Microsoft Office Suite). Preferred Qualifications Teaching, mentoring, and/or service experience at the university level Professional experience in Public Health Experience with USM's Learning Management System, Canvas. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
