    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5637?c=usm": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Division of Marine Science, School of Ocean Science and Engineering",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Division of Marine Science, School of Ocean Science and Engineering | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Adjunct Faculty, Division of Marine Science, School of Ocean Science and Engineering Stennis Space Center, MS, United States | req5637 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Adjunct Faculty, Division of Marine Science, School of Ocean Science and Engineering The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty, Division of Marine Science, School of Ocean Science and Engineering. Position Details Location John C. Stennis Space Center 1020 Balch Blvd Stennis Space Center, Mississippi, 39529 United States Division Marine Science Position Type Faculty Employment Status Part Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Posting Close Date October 20, 2027 Special Instructions to Applications Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary This position is for adjunct teaching opportunities in the Division of Marine Science of the School of Ocean Science and Engineering, which includes academic programs in marine science, hydrographic science, and ocean engineering. Course delivery may occur at either our Stennis Space Center location or our Gulf Park Campus in Long Beach, MS depending on the course. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Deliver course instruction as detailed in course syllabi Course assessments, grading and communications with students Work with teaching assistants, when appropriate, to deliver laboratory/practical sections of courses Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in a related field for undergraduate-level courses and master's degree in a related field for graduate-level courses. Adjunct faculty will need to undergo a faculty qualification assessment to teach each particular course. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Excellent\ncommunication and interpersonal skills. Excellent\nproblem-solving and analytical skills, as well as critical thinking ability. Excellent\norganization skills and attention to detail. Ability to\nwork collaboratively in a team environment. Ability to\nmeet deadlines and work in a multi-priority environment. Ability to\ntreat confidential information with sensitivity. Ability to\neffectively plan work activities, schedules, priorities and utilization of\nresources. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5636?c=usm": {
      "title": "Manager, Network & Telecommunications",
      "description": "Manager, Network & Telecommunications | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Manager, Network & Telecommunications Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5636 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Manager, Network & Telecommunications The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Manager, Network & Telecommunications. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division iTech Administration Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 77,590.00 - 104,973.00 Pay Grade E15 Posting Close Date Five Days After Posted Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary Monitors,\nmaintains, diagnoses and resolves complex hardware and software problems with\nthe University telecommunications system, wide area network, and local area\nnetwork systems and their related services and offerings.  Manages the Telecommunications and Networking\npersonnel by assigning tasks, setting schedules, and resolving basic personnel\nissues.  Job duties are varied and\ncomplex requiring independent judgment.  On-call\nand non-traditional work hours are sometimes required. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Supervises the daily\n     operations of the Networking and Telecommunications staff, including\n     planning, coordinating installation, testing, monitoring, and resolving\n     problems with the University network, cable plant, and communications\n     systems.  Develops training and\n     mentoring programs. Coordinates time off requests, completes personnel\n     actions, and performs annual performance evaluations.  Assures staff maintains the highest\n     level of integrity and professionalism. \n     Participates in the development of schedules, priorities, and\n     determination of time lines and resources. Provides highly skilled\n     technical assistance and knowledgeable advice to users regarding network\n     and telephony hardware and software. \n     Meets periodically with users to discuss current and future network\n     and telephony hardware and software needs. \n     Assists in the development of policies and procedures for users and\n     assures the highest level of customer satisfaction is maintained at all\n     times. Assists in developing and\n     adhering to the annual budget for equipment, services, training, and other\n     needs.  Oversees the organization\n     and tracking of inventory items and ensures adequate spares are available.\n     Verifies that software and hardware maintenance contracts are up to date. Works with directors,\n     other managers, and teams in iTech to discuss solutions to problems and\n     coordinate resources between different groups.  Assists in the formation and\n     implementation of University policies and participates in the Disaster\n     Recovery planning process as it relates to the University communications\n     infrastructure. Tracks changes and\n     developments and provides input to future directions for networking and\n     communication staff.  Keeps informed\n     of national/international computer communication standards and ensures\n     University compliance.  Maintains\n     and/or increases technical knowledge through course work, workshops,\n     seminars and readings. Chairs the university’s\ncabling standards committee to ensure current standards are kept up-to-date\nwith industry standards and best practices. \nResponsible for providing planning and infrastructure design\nrequirements for University infrastructure projects.  Develops and maintains vendor and service\nrelationships. Performs other duties as assigned . Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s\ndegree from an accredited college or university in Electronics Technology or\nComputer Science, or a related information technology field and a minimum of\nfive years of related and progressively more responsible or expansive work\nexperience in an information technology area related to the duties to be\nperformed, including experience overseeing complex or critical information\ntechnology projects, large diverse networks, broadband/baseband data\ncommunications, and multiple contractors and employees.  Directly related experience may be\nsubstituted for the education requirement on a year-for-year basis. Active Cisco Certified Network Professional (CCNP) Valid\ndriver’s license for travel to offices located off the main campus. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Project methodology skills Customer interface skills Ability to lead multi-skilled network technicians Technical skills to work with staff and client Consulting skills to be able to scope projects Advanced network and telecommunication troubleshooting Extensive knowledge of network and telecommunications protocols Extensive experience in troubleshooting and problem solving Extensive knowledge of network hardware and configuration recovery Extensive knowledge of network equipment management and upgrade process Extensive knowledge of network management tools and hardware configuration software Highly motivated and aggressive in enlisting other department’s help in the resolution of communications issues Extensive knowledge of network diagramming tools Ability to mentor staff in areas of expertise Ability to resolve staff conflicts Highly interpersonal and team oriented Preferred Qualifications Network and telephony specific certifications\nare a plus (i.e. Belden-Krone Symphony Certified for copper and fiber, Avaya,\nCisco router and switch certifications). About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5614?c=usm": {
      "title": "Center for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager",
      "description": "Center for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Center for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager Gulfport, MS, United States | req5614 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/20/2026 Back to Search Center for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Center for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager. Position Details Location Marine Research Center 1030 West Pier, Port of Gulfport Gulfport, Mississippi, 39501 United States Division Ocean Enterprise Position Type Staff Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded Yes Salary Range 48,177.00 - 65,180.00 Pay Grade E10 Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Be able to obtain a TWIC (Transportation Identification Credential). Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The\nCenter for Ocean Enterprise Financial Manager provides advanced financial,\nbudgetary, and administrative oversight for all sponsored projects, designated\naccounts, and operational funds associated with the Center. This position\nmanages the financial lifecycle of research programs and Center operations—from\nproposal development through post-award management and final closeout. Responsibilities\ninclude budget development, financial forecasting, cost analysis, account\nreconciliation, internal and external financial reporting, procurement\noversight, and compliance monitoring with federal, state, sponsor, and\nUniversity requirements. The\nFinancial Manager serves as the primary fiscal authority for the Center and\nworks closely with the Executive Director, COE Business Manager, COE\nAdministrative Specialist, principal investigators, external partners, and\nUniversity administrative units to ensure accurate, efficient, and compliant\nfinancial operations. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Develops annual operating budgets for the Center, including forecasting expenditures, revenue projections, cost-share commitments, and indirect cost recovery expectations. Conducts ongoing financial analysis to evaluate Center expenditures and revenue streams, identifying budget risks, spending trends, and financial opportunities. Prepares financial summaries and reports for the Executive Director and internal/external stakeholders. Oversees financial planning associated with leases, tenant agreements, service agreements, and use of Center facilities and resources. Helps oversee development, implementation, and financial management of research projects by creating proposal budgets, submitting internal routing documents, reconciling grants, and preparing financial reports and deliverables.Works closely with external partners and internal teams to prepare BOEs, cost sheets, materials and supply lists, ODC budgets, travel estimates, and labor budgets.Prepares, formats, and submits all required budget and financial documentation for proposal submissions and sponsor requirements. Provides comprehensive financial oversight for all COE grants and contracts, including budgeting, revisions, expenditure tracking, forecasting, and fiscal reporting. Monitors allowability and allocability of expenses and ensures compliance with Uniform Guidance, University policies, and sponsor regulations. Conducts monthly reconciliations of all assigned accounts, verifying accuracy, proper cost classifications, and documentation readiness for audits. Prepares journal entries, salary reallocations, salary verification reports, MDR reconciliations, and other required accounting adjustments. Tracks indirect cost recovery, cost-share commitments, and financial performance metrics for sponsored awards. Collaborates with the COE Administrative Specialist to ensure accurate and timely processing of P-card transactions, journal entries, remittance vouchers and associated financial documentation Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s\nDegree from an accredited college or university in Accounting, Finance,\nBusiness, or related field; and six (6) years of experience in budgeting\nactivities/oversight. Related Education and experience may be substituted on an\nequal basis. Valid Driver’s License is required. US Citizenship Required. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Strong knowledge of financial management, budgeting, and cost principles. Experience with grant accounting and pre/post-award processes. Advanced Excel and financial modeling skills. Ability to interpret financial regulations and sponsor guidelines. Excellent organizational, analytical, and communication skills. Ability to manage multiple deadlines with accuracy and attention to detail. Strong customer service orientation and ability to collaborate across teams. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in Business, Finance, Public Administration, or related field. Experience managing federal grants (NOAA, DoD, NSF, ONR, etc.). Experience with Uniform Guidance, state regulations, and university procurement systems. Familiarity with SOARFIN, enterprise accounting systems, or ERP platforms. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5638?c=usm": {
      "title": "Instructor in Information Technology",
      "description": "Instructor in Information Technology | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Instructor in Information Technology Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5638 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Instructor in Information Technology The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Instructor in Information Technology. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Computing Sciences and Computer Engineering Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date January 15, 2027 Special Instructions to Applicants Undergraduate and Graduate transcripts should be provided with the application. Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the\nUnited States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The\nUniversity will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The School of Computing Sciences and Computer Engineering in the College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Southern Mississippi seeks applications for an Instructor in Information Technology. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teaches twelve hours of undergraduate courses in the information technology discipline each regular semester. Engages in service to the School of Computing Sciences & Computer Engineering Follows the policies and procedures of the School of Computing Sciences and Computer Engineering, College of Arts and Sciences and the University including maintaining office hours and being responsive to student communications Performs other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications Master's degree in information technology or a related discipline. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated ability to teach a broad range of courses within the information technology curriculum, including networking and cybersecurity content. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the college level. Active industry certifications including CompTIA A+,  CompTIA Network+, CompTIA Security+, and/or CompTIA CySA+. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
