    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5632?c=usm": {
      "title": "Professor of Practice in Construction Management",
      "description": "Professor of Practice in Construction Management | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Professor of Practice in Construction Management Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5632 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Professor of Practice in Construction Management The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Professor of Practice in Construction Management. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Construction and Design Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Salary Range 65,000.00 - 65,000.00 Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date Open Until Filled Special Instructions to Applicants Please include a Cover Letter\ndescribing how the candidate's professional background, construction industry\nexperience, and qualifications meet the position's responsibilities; a current\nResume or Curriculum Vitae; a statement describing the applicant's teaching and\nmentoring practices (maximum 2 pages); unofficial transcripts for undergraduate\nand graduate coursework completed; and a list of names and contact information\nfor three professional references. The statement of teaching and\nmentoring practices may draw upon formal classroom instruction or relevant\nprofessional experience, including company-level employee training and\ndevelopment, supervision, coaching, mentoring, or other activities involving the\ntransfer of knowledge and professional skills. Review of applications will begin\nDecember 14, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants must be currently\nauthorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need\nfor visa sponsorship. The University will not sponsor applicants for work visas\n(e.g., H-1B). Please address inquiries\nregarding this search to the chair of the search committee: Dr. Mirsalar Kamari, mirsalar.kamari@usm.edu. Job Summary The School of Construction and Design at The University of Southern Mississippi invites applications for a full-time, nine-month, non-tenure-track faculty position as Professor of Practice in Construction Management, with an anticipated start date of August 16, 2027. This is an on-site position based on the Hattiesburg campus, with primary responsibilities involving face-to-face instruction, potential online teaching assignments, and in-person engagement with students, faculty, and industry partners. The School seeks an accomplished construction professional with substantial industry experience and a strong interest in preparing the next generation of construction professionals. The successful candidate will bring practical knowledge of construction operations, project management, and industry best practices into the classroom. A primary responsibility will be teaching the Construction Management Senior Capstone course, which integrates estimating, scheduling, project management, safety, quality control, and project controls. The School of Construction and Design is home to three accredited undergraduate programs: Construction Management, Architectural Engineering Technology, and Interior Design. The ACCE-accredited Construction Management program offers both on-campus and fully online degree options and maintains strong connections to the construction industry. The School has longstanding relationships with leading construction firms, including Yates Construction, Roy Anderson Corp., Brasfield & Gorrie, Hensel Phelps, and many others. These partnerships support student learning, professional development, internships, and employment opportunities through an active Industry Advisory Council and industry engagement initiatives. Located in the Bobby Chain Technology Center on the Hattiesburg campus, the School provides a dynamic learning environment supported by modern instructional facilities, hands-on learning opportunities, and strong connections with the construction and design industries. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach a full load of undergraduate Construction Management courses each semester, which may include both face-to-face and online instruction, with primary responsibility for the Senior Capstone course, emphasizing the integration and practical application of construction management knowledge and skills. Develop and deliver industry-based learning experiences that integrate construction estimating, scheduling, project management, safety planning, quality assurance and quality control, project controls, and construction documentation. Utilize effective instructional methods and real-world construction project scenarios to ensure course learning outcomes are met and students are prepared for professional practice. Guide and mentor students in developing comprehensive construction project plans, including cost estimates, schedules, safety plans, construction methodologies, and project execution strategies. Coach and mentor Construction Management student teams participating in regional and national construction competitions, with appropriate workload flexibility and travel support provided by the School for these activities. Maintain regular office hours and provide academic guidance and mentoring to students. Support curriculum development, course improvement, student learning outcome assessment, and continuous improvement activities related to ACCE accreditation, including providing end-of-semester course assessment data. Build and maintain strong relationships with construction industry partners to support student projects, internships, experiential learning, and professional development opportunities. Participate in student recruitment, outreach, student organization activities, and other School initiatives. Fulfill institutional service duties within the School, College, University, and community. Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications A bachelor's degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field from an accredited institution. At least five (5) years of professional experience in the United States construction industry. Demonstrated professional experience in construction project management, field operations, preconstruction, or other construction-related responsibilities. Working knowledge of construction estimating, scheduling, project planning, construction safety, cost control, and project execution. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing, and a commitment to collegiality, student learning, and professional mentoring. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities Strong understanding of construction processes, practices, and project delivery methods used in the United States construction industry. Ability to integrate estimating, scheduling, budgeting, safety, quality management, and project controls into comprehensive, project-based learning activities, particularly at the senior capstone level. Ability to incorporate current industry practices, construction technologies, and real-world project experiences into classroom instruction. Ability to guide and mentor students in developing technical, managerial, communication, teamwork, leadership, and problem-solving skills. Ability to establish and maintain productive relationships with industry professionals, organizations, and academic colleagues. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and industry partners. Preferred Qualifications A master's degree in Construction Management, Construction Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related field. Ten (10) or more years of progressively responsible professional experience in the United States construction industry. Significant experience managing construction projects in roles such as Project Manager, Senior Project Manager, Superintendent, Project Executive, Preconstruction Manager, or similar positions. Proficiency with industry-standard construction management software, such as Primavera P6, Microsoft Project, Procore, Bluebeam, or similar applications. Professional certifications or credentials relevant to the construction industry, such as Certified Construction Manager (CCM), Project Management Professional (PMP), OSHA certifications, or similar credentials. Established professional relationships within the construction industry and experience supporting industry partnerships, student internships, or workforce development initiatives. Demonstrated commitment to student success, innovative teaching, continuous improvement, and service to the program. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
    },
    "https://usm.csod.com/ux/ats/careersite/1/home/requisition/5623?c=usm": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design | Job Details Sign In Create Profile English (US) Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design Hattiesburg, MS, United States | req5623 Apply Now Share Save Job Posted on: 10/19/2026 Back to Search Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design The University of Southern Mississippi is currently accepting applications for the position of Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design. Position Details Location Hattiesburg 118 College Drive Hattiesburg, Mississippi, 39406-0001 United States Division School of Performing and Visual Arts Position Type Faculty Employment Status Full Time Grant Funded No Pay Grade Generic Grade Posting Close Date November 9, 2026 Special Instructions to Applicants The Art and Design Program in the School of Performing and Visual Art at The University of Southern Mississippi—an NASAD accredited and Carnegie R1 Top-Tier Research Institution—invites applications for a permanent, non-tenure Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design with an emphasis in Drawing and Painting to start in August 2027. Review of applications will begin November 9, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Please contact Jennifer Courts (jennifer.courts@usm.edu) to inquire about the position. A completed application will include following PDF’s that must be 5mb or smaller: Cover Letter. Title of File: LastName.FirstName_CoverLetter.pdf. Current CV with contact information for three references. Title of File: LastName.FirstName_CV.pdf Artist Statement. Title of File: LastName.FirstName_ArtistStatement.pdf Teaching Philosophy. Title of File: LastName.FirstName_TeachingPhilosophy.pdf Portfolio of twenty samples of the candidate’s personal work demonstrating knowledge & application at a professional level. Title of file: LastName.FirstName_PersonalWork.pdf. Each work in the portfolio must be labeled with title, size, medium, and date.  Please include an inventory list of the work at the end of the document. Portfolio of twenty samples of the candidate’s student work from relevant courses. Title of file: Lastname.FirstName_StudentWork.pdf. Each work in the portfolio must be labeled with title, size, medium, date, and course of instruction. Please include an inventory list of the work at the end of the document. A single PDF containing sample syllabi from relevant courses that the candidate has experience teaching. A single PDF containing sample assignments from relevant courses. Academic Transcripts (unofficial transcripts are acceptable until final hiring process). Applicants must be currently authorized to work in the United States on a full-time basis without the need for visa sponsorship. The University will not sponsor applicants for work visas (e.g., H-1B). Job Summary The Art and Design program seeks applicants for a full-time, 9-month faculty position with a 4/4 course load at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor of Art and Design. The successful applicant will be prepared to teach 2D design, color design and all levels of undergraduate drawing and painting, with the potential to also teach printmaking. Participation in Art and Design activities and service to the program, school, college and university is expected. Primary Duties and Responsibilities Teach undergraduate courses in Studio Art in Art and Design. Advise and mentor undergraduate art majors. Attend all faculty/staff, school, and area meetings. Engage in recruitment as well as service to the program, school, and university. Teach a 4/4 course load. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications M.F.A. in Studio Art or relevant area. Knowledge, Skills & Abilities Comprehensive knowledge and skill to teach courses in foundations drawing, and upper-level undergraduate courses in drawing, painting, and printmaking; course content areas include but are not limited to 2D composition (linear and tonal), working from direct observation, figure anatomy and structure, and visual form problem solving. Preferred Qualifications Ability to teach all forms of printmaking. About The University of Southern Mississippi Since our founding in 1910, The University of Southern\nMississippi has remained dedicated to preparing\nstudents for success. We deliver programs to more than 13,000 students\nin Hattiesburg and Long Beach, at teaching and research sites across the\nMississippi Gulf Coast, as well as online. We\nare a community-engaged Carnegie R1 university, earning distinction as one of\nthe nation's leading research institutions. Southern Miss is known for pioneering work in\npolymer science, ocean science, spectator sports safety and security, and bringing\nlanguage to children with communication disorders. We are also a national\nleader in a broad range of disciplines, including cybersecurity, hydrography,\nnutrition, aquaculture, kinesiology, and economic development, among others. We produce graduates ready to enter\nfields that are leading the way in emerging technologies through programs such\nas computer engineering, information technology, and ocean engineering. We’re developing the next generation of\nbusiness leaders, while also responding to critical workforce shortages by\nproducing skilled professionals in education and nursing. With a tradition of\nexcellence in the arts, we are one of only 36 public institutions in the nation\naccredited in four major areas of the arts. Home to the Golden Eagles, our\nstudent-athletes compete in 17 NCAA Division I sports. With a culture marked by passion and\npersistence, Southern Miss is delivering graduates who are ready for life. For more information, visit www.usm.edu . The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment. EOE/VETS/DISABILITY. Apply Now Share Save Job Equal Opportunity Statement The University of Southern Mississippi is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, disability, age, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information. The University is committed to providing access, equal opportunity and reasonable accommodation for individuals with disabilities in employment, its service, programs, and activities. If reasonable accomodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, to perform essential job functions, and/or to receive other beneifts and privileges of employment, please contact: The Office of Equal Employment Opportunity & Labor Regulatory Compliance eeo@usm.edu McLemore Hall (MCL) 310 | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 Phone: 601.266.4050 | Fax: 601.266.4541 | TTY/TDD: 1.800.582.2233 www.usm.edu/equal-employment Employment Notices Federal law requires all employers to verify the identity and employment eligibility of all persons hired to work in the United States. Click on the links below to learn more about employer requirements and your right to work: E-Verify Poster Right to Work Poster Employee Rights - Family and Medical Leave Act Employee Rights - Employee Polygraph Protection Act If you have questions, please email the Human Resources department at jobs@usm.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report The\n University of Southern Mississippi is committed to the safety and \nsecurity of the USM community. The annual federal required compliance \ndocument which contains policy statements and crime statistics for the \nUniversity is available on the UPD website at http://www.usm.edu/police/ .\n You may also request a copy by contacting the University Police \nDepartment at Bond Hall, 1st Floor West, Hattiesburg, MS 39406 (601) 266-\n 4986. The policy statements address the University's policies, \nprocedures and programs concerning safety and security, for example, \npolicies for responding to emergency situations and sexual offenses. \nThree years' of statistics are included for certain types of crimes that\n were reported to have occurred on campus, in or on off-campus buildings\n or property owned or controlled by the University and on public \nproperty within or immediately adjacent to the campus. University Human Resources | 118 College Drive #5111 | Hattiesburg, MS 39406 USM Home Page | USM HR | About Hattiesburg if you have questions please email: jobs@usm.edu"
